(2104, 190, 3, 'There are 10 houses (numbered 1 to 10) that have equal number of bread slices.  House No. 1 gives a slice of bread each, to all the houses numbered after it (i.e., from 2 to 10). House No.2 gives a slice of bread each to all the houses numbered after it (i.e., from 3 to 10). The next two houses continue this type of distribution. In the end, the total sum of bread slices with the houses that gave bread to the other houses is half the number of bread slices with the houses that did not give any bread. What was the original number of bread slices in each house? ', '36', '48', '42', '30', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
