(2112, 190, 2, 'The population of a town increases by 10% every year. If the difference between the population two years and one year ago was 11000, what is the present population of the town?', '143,000', '121000	', '133100		', '123000', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2113, 190, 2, 'The length of a rectangle is increased by 18% and its breadth is decreased by 15%. What is the percentage increase/decrease in the area of the rectangle?', '0.3% increase 	', '35.7% increase	', '5.7% decrease ', '30.3% decrease', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2114, 190, 1, 'The sum of two numbers is 5 and the reciprocal of one of the numbers exceeds the reciprocal of the other by the product of their reciprocals. What is the product of the reciprocals of the two numbers?', '3', '1/5', '1/6', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2115, 190, 1, 'For a body starting from rest, the distance travelled (d) is directly proportional to the square of the time elapsed from the start (t). When t = 4 sec, d = 48 m. What is the value of d (in m) at t = 6 sec?', '108 ', '144', '115 	', '147', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2116, 190, 2, 'The kinetic energy of a body is directly proportional to the square of its speed when the mass is kept constant and is proportional to mass when its speed is kept constant. A body with a mass of 4kg and a speed of 10 m/s has a kinetic energy of 200 joules. What is the kinetic energy (in joules) of a body whose mass is 10 kg and speed is 5 m/s?', '125', '1250', '25', '250', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2117, 190, 1, 'The ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls in a school is 6 : 5. If an additional 18 girls were to join the class, the ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls would become 3 : 4. What is the initial number of girls in the class?', '34', '36', '40', '30', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2118, 190, 1, 'If 4 is subtracted from the numerator and 1 is added to the denominator of a fraction, the new fraction formed is 1/2. If 2 is added to the numerator of the initial fraction, the ratio of the new numerator to the denominator becomes 1:1. Find the original fraction. ', '11/13', '18/23', '13/15', '5/14', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2119, 190, 2, 'The ratio of Arun''s age to Varun''s age is same as the ratio of the ages of their respective elder brothers. The ratio of the difference of the ages of Arun and Varun to that of the difference of the ages of their respective brothers is 1: 3. What is the ratio of the sum of the ages of their respective brothers to the sum of the ages of Arun and Varun? ', '6:1', '4:1	', '3:1	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2120, 190, 1, 'X is directly proportional to a quantity which is 5 more than the square of Y. X is 56 when Y is 3. What is the positive value of Y when X is 84?', '29', '4', '15', '6', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2121, 190, 2, 'Three different types of pens priced at Rs.5, Rs.8 and Rs.13 per piece are displayed in three different boxes by a trader. Mr. Sharma bought from this shop all three types of pens, spending a total sum of Rs.1152. The numbers of the pens he bought, taken in the order in which the prices are mentioned above, are in the ratio 5 : 4 : 3. How many pens of the costliest variety did he buy?', '156 	', '96 ', '36	', '60', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2122, 190, 2, 'The volume of a cone varies as the square of the radius of its base when its height is fixed and also varies as its height when radius of its base is fixed. If a radius of 5 cm and height of 8 cm give it a volume of 78 cubic centimeters, then what will be the radius (in cm) if the cone has a height of 5 cm and a volume of 195 cubic centimeters?', '9', '15', '20', '10', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2123, 190, 2, 'What must be subtracted from p and added to q so that the ratio of the resultants becomes 1 : 4?', '(p + q)/4		', '(4p â€“ q)/5', '(p â€“ q)/ (p + q)', '(p â€“ q)/4', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2124, 191, 2, 'In 2008, the price of a mobile phone increases by 20% with respect to that in 2007. By what percentage is its price in 2007 less than that in 2008?', '15%	', '16.67%	', '13.33%	', '20%', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2125, 191, 2, 'Abhishek secures 42% of the total marks in an exam and gets 29 marks more than the pass mark. Anirban secures 29% of the total marks in the same exam and fails by 23 marks. What is the pass mark as a percentage of the total marks?', '28%', '32.25%	', '34.75%	', '35%', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
