(2128, 191, 2, 'The cost of production of a Rolex watch which is sold at 35% profit went up by 28%. What should be the percentage increase in the selling price to maintain the profit percentage the same even at the new cost of production? ', '28% ', '35% ', '63% 		', '50%', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2129, 191, 2, 'The success rate, at one stage, of the Indian cricket team in Australia was 25% from 60 matches. If 54 matches were played since then, how many more matches would India have lost if its overall success rate is 50%? ', '12 	', '14 		', '18 	', '22', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2130, 191, 2, 'Due to inflation the total cost of monthly household items has gone up by 25%, but the salary of the Gupta had increased by only 20%. Initially, Gupta is used to spend 40% of the salary on household items. What percentage of the present salary would Gupta spend to buy the same quantities of household items?', '40%', '41.33% ', '41.67%		', '42%', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2131, 191, 3, 'In 2000, Abhilash paid a tax of 20% of his salary. In 2001, his salary increased by 33.33% and the tax scheme changed. Under the new tax scheme, he had to pay a fixed sum of Rs. 1500 and an additional 20% on the amount above Rs. 10000. If he is paying Rs. 100 more in taxes, under the new scheme, what is his salary (in Rs.) in 2001?', '20000', '18000', '14400', '12000', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2132, 191, 3, 'The price of an LED TV has been decreasing every year by a constant percentage over the last 4 years. If the cost of the LED TV was Rs. 150000, 4 years ago and it costs Rs. 98415 now, then find the annual rate of decrease.', '8% 	', '5% 		', '10% ', '15%', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2133, 191, 2, 'If the area of a rectangle is increased by 56% and its breadth is increased by 20%, what is the percentage increase in its perimeter?', '20% ', '24%	', '30%	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2134, 191, 2, 'St Maryâ€™s Public School has 30% more students than St Josephâ€™s Public School. If 60 students move from St Maryâ€™s Public School to St Josephâ€™s Public School, the two schools will have the same number of students. What is the sum of the present number of students in both the schools? ', '600', '400', '800', '920', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2135, 191, 3, 'Sharmaâ€™s tutorial centre was started in the year 2004. Every year a certain number of students enrol for class XII tutorials. This number increases by 20% every year. If the number of students in the year 2008 is 576 more than the number of students in the year 2007, how many students enrolled in the year 2005? ', '2000', '2160', '2340', '2400', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2136, 191, 3, 'Rocket Singh is a salesman and has to choose between two schemes of remuneration. Scheme I has a fixed salary of Rs. 3700 and a commission of 2% on sales above Rs. 50000. Scheme II has no fixed salary, but offers 3% commission on the sales for the first Rs. 50000 or part thereof, increases at the rate of 1 percentage point for every increase of Rs. 50000 or part there of sales, upto a maximum of 20% of sales. What is the minimum value of the sales (in Rs.) above which he can prefer Scheme II?', '50000	', '89000	', '140000	', 'No such sales value exists.', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2137, 191, 2, 'Initially a discount of 30% was being offered on a refrigerator. The dealer increased the discount further by 20%, because the customer bargained. If the selling price of the television is Rs. 11200, then what is its marked price (in Rs.)?', '19200	', '16000	', '20000	', '24000', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2138, 191, 2, 'Out of 150 watermelons, when 30 watermelons were rotten, the selling price of each of the remaining watermelons is increased by 25% to retain the original 25% profit. What is the overall profit or loss percentage if the remaining watermelons were sold at the original selling price? ', '0%	', ' 6.66% profit', '6.25% loss	', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
