(2173, 194, 3, 'Gopi, Murthy and Hari had some amount of money. Gopi gives half his amount to Murthy, who then gives half of what he now has to Hari. Hari gives half of what he now has to Gopi, who now has exactly the same amount what he started with. If the sum of Murthyâ€™s initial amount and twice Hariâ€™s initial amount is Rs. 15, what was the amount (in rupees) Gopi started with? ', '10', '15', '30', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2174, 194, 3, 'A person on an exercise regime decides to lose 500 calories in a day. For every 30 minutes of exercise he loses 80 calories, but gains 40 calories per cake that he eats. In the morning he exercises for a certain time and he eats a certain number of cakes. In the afternoon he exercises for double the time but eats thrice the number of cakes. In the evening he exercises for 1.5 times the time he spends in the morning session and eats 4 times the number of cakes he eats in the morning. Had he not eaten any cake, he would have exceeded his target by 220 calories. If he actually falls short of his target by 180 calories, then, what is the number of cakes he has eaten in the afternoon? ', '12', '16', '6', '10', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2175, 194, 2, 'A man wins a bet and the amount gets doubled. Thrice the numerical value of the sum of his age (in years) and the numerical value of the original amount with him is 200 more than the numerical value of the sum of his age and that of the money after winning. He bets the new amount and it doubles again. Now, twice the sum of the numerical value of the amount before the first bet and the numerical value of his age (in years) is 100 less than the sum of the numerical value of his age (in years) and that of the final amount after the second winning. Find the initial amount with the man (all amounts are in Rupees) ', '40', '60', '80', '50', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2176, 195, 3, 'Seven cats and twelve rats are divided into two groups each containing at least 1 cat and 1 rat. If the number of cats in the first group is more than the number of rats in that group, what is the least number by which rats exceed cats in the second group?', '5', '7', '6', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
