(2183, 196, 1, 'Dilip and Samrat can do a piece of work in 16 days and 24 days respectively. Samrat works alone for 15 days and leaves. In how many days can Dilip complete the remaining work?', '8', '10', '6', '7', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2184, 196, 1, 'Mihir can build a wall in 18 days and Sabari can do the same in 30 days. After Mihir had built half the wall, Sabari joins him. What is the total number of days taken to build the wall completely?', '13', '14 5/8 	', '15  1/2 	', '16', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `qb_options` (`id`, `cat_id`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `answer1`, `answer2`, `answer3`, `answer4`, `answer5`, `option1`, `option2`, `option3`, `option4`, `option5`, `status`) VALUES
(2185, 196, 2, 'A team of two people Madan and Karthik, who can complete a piece of work together in 40 days, begin the work. Ritesh joins them after 8 days and the work gets completed in 24 days after Ritesh joins them. In how many days can Ritesh alone complete the entire work?', '100', '80', '90', '120', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2186, 196, 2, 'Santosh can do a piece of work in 40 days and Satish can do the same in 60 days. Santosh works on alone for a few days. Then Satish joins him and together they complete the work 10 days earlier than the time Santosh alone would have taken. After how many days did Satish join Santosh?', '19', '12', '20', '15', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2187, 196, 2, 'The cost of grass for 30 cows and 45 goats for 30 days is Rs. 1080. If 30 goats eat double the amount of grass eaten by 20 cows, what is the cost of grass (in Rs.) eaten by 20 goats in 15 days? ', '200', '160', '240', '100', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2188, 196, 1, 'A gas station needs 56 men to fill air in 20,000 tires in 72 days. How many men does the gas station need to fill air in 30,000 tires in 63 days?', '120', '108', '96', '144', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2189, 196, 3, 'Yash can do a piece of work in half the time taken by Ramesh. Kaushik can do the same work in one-third the time taken by Yash. All three of them work on it for 40 days, after which, Ramesh leaves. Kaushik and Yash complete the remaining work in 15 more days. How many days would it take for Yash alone to complete the total work?', '80', '480', '240', '160', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2190, 196, 2, 'A machine X has to manufacture 1000 bolts, which it can do in 40 days. It breaks down after working for10 days. A machine Y completes the remaining work in 15 days. How many bolts can be manufactured by both of them in 40 days?', '3000', '4500', '6000', '2500', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2191, 196, 2, 'Machines A, B and C can do a piece of work in 30, 45 and 90 days respectively. A, B and C start the work together. A goes out of order after 6 days. After 8 more days, B and C also go out of order. A got repaired by then and it completes the remaining work. What portion of the total work did machine A do?', '3/4', '8/15 ', '4/9	', '3/5', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2192, 196, 2, 'Bharat and Bhaskar together complete half the work in 18 days. Bhaskar and Bhushan complete the remaining half in 12 days. If Bharat alone can complete the work in 72 days, in how many days can Bhushan alone complete the work?', '72', '42', '36', '45', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2193, 196, 2, 'In a garments factory, a group of 50 tailors plan to achieve their target for the next 30 days by working 12 hours a day. Due to various reasons they put in only 10 hours a day for the first 15 days. Now, if â€˜xâ€™ men leave and the rest continue working for only 10 hours a day, it takes 35 days more than the initially estimated time to meet the target. How many men were left after 15 days?', '20', '21', '25', '29', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2194, 196, 3, 'A group of laborers are building a villa. After half the villa has been built, double the number of laborers joins the original group. The villa gets completed 8 days earlier. What is the total number of days needed to complete the wall by the initial group of men?', '12', '24', '16', '18', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2195, 197, 3, 'A man builds 1/8th of the part of a wall every day. Out of the length of the wall built per day, 20% falls off each day. In how many days can he complete the wall, if the wall once complete cannot fall? ', '91/4 ', '10	', '11', '94/5', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2196, 196, 2, 'Tarun is one and a half times more efficient than Varun. Tarun can do a piece of work in 20 days. What portion of the total work can both of them together complete in 8 days?', '3/5	', '5/6 ', '2/3	 ', '1/2', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2197, 196, 2, 'Gautam and Ganesh can complete a piece of work in 12 days, Ganesh and Gaurav in 20 days and Gautam and Gaurav in 15 days. In how many days, respectively, can Gautam, Ganesh and Gaurav complete the work if they work individually?', '20, 30, 60', '45, 60, 180	', '30, 45, 90		', '45, 60, 20', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2198, 196, 3, 'Working alone, Shruti, Smriti and Sukriti can do a piece of work in 10, 15 and 30 days respectively. All three of them start the work together, but after â€˜xâ€™ days Shruti leaves and then after â€˜yâ€™ more days Smriti leaves and Sukriti completes the remaining work. If Smriti had not left, Sukriti and Smriti would have completed the remaining work in (y + 3) days after Shruti had left. If both Shruti and Smriti had stayed, the work would have been completed in (x + 3) days. What is the total number of days taken to complete the work?', '10', '14', '8', '15', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2199, 196, 2, 'Mukesh and Brijesh together repair an old building in 36 days and receive Rs. 10800. If Brijesh is three times as efficient as Mukesh, how much does he earn (in Rs.) in 8 days? ', '1600', '1800', '2000', '2200', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2200, 196, 2, 'Arjun can alone complete a piece of work in 9 days and Bheem alone can complete it in 12 days. Consider two cases in which the two work on alternate days: Case-1: Arjun starts the work; Case-2: Bheem starts the work. What is the difference between the time taken in both the cases? ', '1/3 days', '1/4 days', '1 day', '1/12 days', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2201, 196, 3, 'The efficiency of a man is reduced by half every two and a half hours. At maximum efficiency, he could have completed the job in 150 hours. How many hours does it take him to complete the job if his efficiency becomes maximum after every 10 hours, and then reduces as mentioned above?', '300', '320', '600', '620', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2202, 198, 3, 'Sudheer, Rajveer and Sandesh divide a work amongst themselves in the ratio of 2 : 3 : 5. Their rates of work are in the ratio 1:2:3. It takes Sudheer 12 days to complete his part. What is the amount of work completed by them in 3 days from the start?', '3/10	', '11/45', '3/5		', '31/45', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2203, 198, 2, 'If there is one man less to do a certain work, then the number of days required to complete the work would be one more. If the initial number of man-days required to complete the work is 72, how many worked initially?', '6', '8', '9', '14', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2204, 198, 2, 'A piece of work when done by a man, a woman and a child costs Rs.480, Rs.540 and Rs.720 respectively. Their respective daily wages are Rs.40, Rs.30 and Rs.20. If all the three are employed   to do the work, how much would it cost to complete the work (in Rs.)?', '720', '520', '540', '400', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2205, 198, 2, 'In 10 days, Dan can do as much work as John can do in 15 days. To do a certain job both together take 42 days. In how many days can John, working alone, complete the job?', '70', '105', '108', '120', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2206, 198, 3, 'Girish and Deepak agree to complete a piece of work in 30 days. They also agree to forfeit double the amount of wages corresponding to the uncompleted part of work, if they fail to complete the work in time. If Girish alone can complete the work in 60 days and they lost 1/3rd of the pay due for the total-work, in how many days can Deepak alone complete the work?', '45', '90', '60', '120', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2207, 198, 2, 'Pranav, Salma and Sundar, each working alone, take 20 days, 10 days and 5 days respectively to make 2000 hats each. If the defects in their production are 10%, 20% and 40% respectively, how many non-defective hats can they make in 20 days? ', '9800', '10000', '9000', '10200', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2208, 198, 2, 'The work done by a woman in 6 days is equal to the work done by two girls in 8 days. How many women are needed to do a piece of work in 48 days which 72 girls can do in 16 days? ', '8', '9', '10', '11', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2209, 198, 3, 'Raghu takes 20% less time than Vijay to do the work.  Raghu and Vijay complete the job together in 6 days if their efficiencies remain constant. Vijay alone starts the work. If beginning with the second day, the amount of work Vijay can do per day keeps doubling compared to the previous day, then on which day from the start would Vijay complete the work? ', '4th 	', '3rd  	', '5th  ', '2nd ', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2210, 198, 2, 'Vishwas starts a piece of work. Starting from the second day onwards, every day a new man joins. With every new man joining, the work that each man (that was previously on the job) can do per day doubles. The work is completed in 6 days. On which day would they have completed the work, if the work that each of them could do per day had remained constant?', '20th day', '21st day	', '16th day', '15th day', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2211, 198, 3, 'It takes Kamal, Vimal and Vipul 36, 48 and 72 days respectively to do a piece of work. Each of them does the same amount of work and they complete the work in 52 days. Instead, if Vimal did extra work equal to the sum of the parts of the works done by Kamal and Vipul, they could have completed the work one day earlier. How much more work did Vimal do in the second case as compared to that done by him in the first case?', '1/9	', '1/6 ', '1/4 		', '1/3', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2212, 198, 2, 'Harini, Damini and Suhasini can do a piece of work in 8, 16 and 24 days respectively. They begin a new job of similar nature and each of them works on it for one third of the total period of work. If they get Rs. 7700 for the new job, how much should Damini get (in Rs.) given that the amounts distributed are in proportion to the amounts of work done?', '1300', '2100', '3900', '2400', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2213, 198, 3, 'Jadeja, Bhangar, Balaji and Dravid can do a piece of work in 8, 16, 32 and 64 days respectively. Dravid starts the work and Balaji joins him after 1/4th of the work is done. Bhangar joins them after half the work is done and Jadeja joins them after 3/4th work is done. On which day from the start of the work, will they complete the work? ', '30th 		', '32nd 	', '25th		', '24th ', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2214, 198, 3, 'If a piece of work can be done by 8 men and 7 women in 12 days or by 10 men and 26 women in 5 days, in how many days can  45 men do a piece of work thrice as large?', '8', '10', '12', '15', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2215, 198, 2, 'Spoorti can complete a piece of work in 14 days, while Shreya and Shweta can do it in 21 days each. Spoorti works on the first day. Spoorti and Shreya work on the second day and Spoorti, Shreya and Shweta work on the third day. Also Spoorti works on the fourth day, Spoorti and Shreya work on the fifth day and Spoorti, Shreya and Shweta work on the sixth day and this cycle continues till the work is completed. In how many days is the work completed?', '8', '8 4/7 ', '9', '10 3/7    ', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2216, 198, 2, 'A pipe can fill a tank in 6 hours, while a leak which is at one-third the height of the tank can empty upto that part in 2 hours. If both are operated simultaneously and initially the tank is full, then when will it be one-third full?', '2 hours', '2 1/3 hours', '1 1/2 hours		', '4 hours', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2217, 198, 2, 'A man, a woman and a boy can do a piece of work in 6, 8 and 12 days respectively. If a man and a woman start the work, how many boys should join them on the second day to complete the work on the same day? ', '5', '4', '2', '1', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2218, 198, 2, 'Two pipes P and Q can fill a cistern in 10 and 15 hours respectively. Both the pipes were opened at 09:00 a.m. and the cistern was full at 4:30 p.m. What could be the minimum possible duration for which one of the pipes must have been closed during that interval?', '4 hours	', '2.5 hours		', '2 hours	', '4/3 hours', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2219, 199, 3, 'There are â€˜tâ€™ taps numbered 1, 2 and so on till â€˜tâ€™, each of which can fill a cistern. The rate of filling of the nth tap is such that it is equal to twice that of all the taps from 1 to (n â€“ 1) put together. If the 18th tap can fill the empty cistern in 2 seconds, then what is the approximate time in which the 14th tap alone can fill the empty cistern?', '3 minutes 21 seconds	', '2 minutes 42 seconds', '3 minutes 11 seconds', '3 minutes 45 seconds', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2220, 198, 3, 'P and Q are filling pipes which can fill a tank in 15 and 20 minutes respectively. R is an emptying pipe which can empty the full tank in 30 minutes. The three pipes are operated continuously one after the other in the order of P, Q and R, each being kept opened for x minutes until the tank is filled. If the tank is full after 322/3 minutes, then what is the value of x?', '1', '2', '3', '4', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2221, 198, 3, 'Govinda, Syed and Janak can complete a piece of work in 20, 30 and 24 days respectively. All three of them started working and after a certain number of days (y), Govinda stopped working and Syed stopped working exactly (y) days before the work got completed. In how many integral numbers of days was the work completed?', '12', '16', '14', '20', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2222, 200, 3, 'Farooq works 2/3 times as fast as Ashwin and Lalith together. Farooq and Lalith together work twice as fast as Ashwin. If Lalith alone takes 15 days to complete a job, how (in days) long would Farooq and Ashwin individually take to complete the job?', '10, 12', '12, 10	', '15, 20		', '20, 15', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2223, 200, 2, '2 men or 5 women can complete a piece of work in 27 days. In how many days can 4 men and 5 women complete the same work?', '8', '7', '9', '5', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2224, 201, 3, 'A number of crabs are kept in a jar of height 40 cm. One crab climbs up by 3 cm in a minute and in the subsequent minute it is pulled down by the other crabs by 1 cm. If this cycle of alternate up and down movements of the crab repeats until it reaches the top, in how many minutes will the crab reach the top of the jar? (Assume that once it reaches the top it is not pulled down)?', '40 minutes		', '39 minutes	', '38 2/3 minutes', '37 1/3 minutes', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2225, 200, 1, 'The work done by Arvind in 12 hours is equal to the work done by Prabin in 15 hours, which in turn is equal to the work done by Nitin in 20 hours. They undertook a particular work and finished the work, working together in 15 hours. In how many hours can each of them, working alone, complete the same work?', '20, 30, 40	', '30, 40, 20', '30, 24, 40		', '36, 45, 60', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2226, 200, 2, 'A swimming pool is fitted with three pipes with uniform rates of flow. The first two pipes operating simultaneously can fill the pool in half the time that the third pipe alone takes to fill the tank. The second pipe, to fill the pool, takes 18 hours more than the first pipe working alone and 12 hours more than the third pipe working alone. Find the time taken by the three pipes individually to fill the pool (in hours).', '12, 16, 18 ', '16, 28, 20', '18, 36, 24		', '8, 20, 12', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2227, 200, 3, 'Krishna and Sahil can complete a piece of work individually in 36 days and 54 days respectively. They work on alternate days starting with Krishna. Further, they get a holiday after every four days and after the holiday the person who worked on the last day before the holiday now starts the work. After how many days from the start will the work get completed? ', '54', '52', '531/3', '53', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2228, 200, 2, 'A pipe is filling a tank of 300 liters capacity at 6 liters/hr. Because of a leak it takes 40 hours more to fill the tank. What is the rate (in liters/hr) at which water is leaking?', '4', '3', '2.67', '2.33', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2229, 200, 2, 'Two pipes A and B which can fill a tank in 21 and 28 hours respectively were opened simultaneously. But there was a leak and it took 2 hours more to fill the tank. In how many hours can the leak empty the full tank?', '42', '63', '84', '98', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2230, 200, 2, 'A tank is full of water. A drain pipe, which can empty the full tank in 40 minutes, is opened. 24 minutes later another pipe which can fill the empty tank in 20 minutes is opened. After how much time (since the filling pipe is opened) is the tank full again (in minutes)?', '18', '24', '36', '40', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2231, 200, 3, 'Three taps â€˜xâ€™, â€˜yâ€™ and â€˜zâ€™ can fill a tank in 18, 24 and 36 hours respectively. â€˜xâ€™ was opened first, â€˜yâ€™ was opened after time â€˜tâ€™ and â€˜zâ€™ was opened after â€˜2tâ€™, measured from the time x was opened. If the time taken for the tank to fill up is 3 hours less than double the time that it would have taken, had â€˜xâ€™, â€˜yâ€™, â€˜zâ€™ been opened simultaneously, what is the time (in hours) after which â€˜yâ€™ was opened?', '4', '6 3/7 ', '4 1/5 	', '', '5', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2232, 200, 3, 'In a late night party, attended by 130 people, each of the persons numbered from 1 to 130, takes as many shots as the number of factors of his/ her number. What is the maximum number of shots taken by any person?', '12', '15', '16', '18', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2233, 200, 2, 'The remainder when the sum 1!2! + 3!4! + 5!6! +â€¦â€¦.+ 999!1000! is divided by 15 is', '4', '11', '13', '0', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2234, 200, 3, 'The number of factors of a natural number N is 20. Which of the following is/are the possible number of prime factors the number N can have?<br>\r\n(A) 1			(B) 2				(C) 3 				(D) 4\r\n', 'only A and B', 'only B and C', 'only A, B and C', 'A, B, C and D', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2235, 200, 3, 'Two cattle with same capacity to eat are tied to a pair of diagonal corners of a rectangular field of dimensions 28 m Ã— 14 m using ropes of length 14 m each. If the grass available to the cattle is sufficient to survive them for 11 days, how many more days can they survive if the cattle are left loose at the end of the 10th day after they started grazing? ', '2', '3', '4', 'more than 4 ', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2236, 200, 2, 'The unitâ€™s digit of a two-digit number is 2 less than its tenâ€™s digit. If the number is not less than 7 times the sum of its digits, find the sum of all such possible numbers.', '51', '93', '146', 'None of these', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2237, 202, 3, 'If P, Q, R are three angles of a triangle such that cosP+cosQ+cosR> cosPÃ—cosQÃ—cosR  , then which of the following statements is/are true?<br>\r\n(A) PQR is an acute angled triangle	<br>		(B) PQR is a right angled triangle<br>\r\n(C) PQR is an obtuse angled triangle \r\n', 'only A and B ', 'only B and C  ', 'A, B and C    ', 'Only A and C', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2238, 202, 3, 'An absent minded professor tried to calculate the sum of all composite numbers between 20 and 60. He miscalculated the answer as 1560.What was his mistake?', 'He added exactly 3 primes between 20 and 40', 'He added exactly 4 primes between 40 and 60', 'He added all the primes between 20 and 60', 'Except one, he added all the primes between 20 and 60', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2239, 202, 3, 'An amount of Rs. 1435 is divided among 5 persons in such a way that one-fifth of the first personâ€™s share is equal to five times the share of the second person, which is equal to Rs. 5 less than the share of third person, which is equal to Rs. 5 more than the share of the fourth person, which is equal to the share of the fifth person. Which of the following options is definitely false?', 'The combined share of the 1st and 3rd persons is more than that of the 2nd and 4th persons.', 'The second person is the one that gets the least share', 'The third person gets Rs. 10 less than the fourth person', 'The share of the fifth person is Rs. 185', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2240, 202, 2, 'The difference of an odd and an even function is ', 'always an odd function	', 'always an even function', 'neither odd nor even function ', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2241, 202, 3, 'If (p + q + r + s)/(a + b + c + d + e + f)= X, where p,q,r,s are four consecutive odd integers and a,b,c,d,e,f are six consecutive even integers. If p= 2n+1, where n is a positive integer, then which of the following is a possible value of X?', '(n+2)/2n 	', '4(n+2)/3(2n+5)  	', '(2n+1)/2n 	', '(n+2)/5(2n+5) ', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2242, 202, 2, 'A car is racing on a circular track of radius 105m. What is the average speed of the car (in m/s) if it covers 960Â° in 80 seconds?', '22', '20', '18', '14', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2243, 202, 2, 'Four friends Ajay, Badal, Chirag and Diya have some marbles among themselves. Diya gives 3 times as many marbles as each of the others already had. Badal then gives 20 marbles to each of his friends. Ajay then doubles the number of marbles present with each of his friends. Finally each of them has 80 marbles. How many marbles does Chirag have initially?', '45', '25', '20', '5', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2244, 202, 2, 'Four friends Ajay, Badal, Chirag and Diya have some marbles among themselves. Diya gives 3 times as many marbles as each of the others already had. Badal then gives 20 marbles to each of his friends. Ajay then doubles the number of marbles present with each of his friends. Finally each of them has 80 marbles. How many marbles did Diya distribute to her friends?', '225', '245', '200', '185', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2245, 202, 3, 'If a,b,c,d are even numbers and p,q,r,s are odd numbers then which of the following can never be true?', '(a+b)/p=cqr ', 'd+pqr=ab+bc ', 'p+q=a+b+c+d', 'pqrd=abcs ', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2246, 202, 1, 'The number of positive integers less than or equal to 1000, which are divisible by 3, 5 and 7 is', '3', '4', '8', '9', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2247, 202, 2, 'An ant is climbing down a pole inclined at an angle of 60Â° to the ground at a speed of 0.5 feet/sec. How fast is the ant approaching the ground (in feet/sec)?', 'âˆš3/4 	', 'âˆš3/2 	', '1/âˆš2 ', '1/2', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2248, 202, 2, 'The ratio of the distances covered by Vel and Vivek , with their respective speeds of â€˜uâ€™ kmph and â€˜vâ€™ kmph, in a certain time of t seconds is 3:4. In a 1000 m race, if Vivek gives Vel a head start of â€˜xâ€™ m, what is the value of â€˜xâ€™ such that both of them reach the finishing line at the same time?', '125', '250', '300', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2249, 202, 3, 'A seagull, flying at a uniform speed, moves from the bow (front end of a ship) to the stern (rear end of a ship) in one-third of the time it takes to move from the stern to the bow of the same ship, sailing at 10 m/s  downstream. What are the speeds of the seagull (in m/s) relative to the ship?', '10, 30', '10, 20', '15, 30', '20, 30', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2250, 202, 1, 'A ball thrown up 12 feet into the air bounces back to half its previous height every time it hits the ground. What is the total distance travelled by the ball (approximately, in feet)?', '24', '48', '12', '18', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2251, 203, 2, 'A person travels from point X and travels south 9.5 miles. Then he turns east and travels 4 miles. He then turns north and travels 6.5 miles and returns to X in a straight line. If he is travelling at 20 miles per hour, what is the total time taken (in minutes) by him for this round trip?', '48', '65', '60', '75', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2252, 202, 2, 'A person invests Rs. 1.5 lakh in real-estate and Rs. 2.5 lakh in silver. Real-estate appreciated by 6% and the silver depreciated. If he sold both these assets and made an overall loss of 3.5%, what percent did silver depreciate by?', '9%', '10%	', '9.2%', '8.8%', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2253, 203, 2, 'In a race, Sunny was not first. Jatin came in after Dan, Hemant was not ahead of Rahul. Sunny was not in front of Jatin. Hemant was not fourth or fifth. Rahul was not first. Who finished first and second in the race?', 'Dan followed by Rahul', 'Dan followed by Jatin', 'Dan followed by Sunny		', 'Cannot be determined from the clues.', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2254, 205, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Each question consists of 5 statements followed by options consisting of 3 statement put together in a specific order.  Choose the option which indicates a valid argument, that is, where the third statement is a conclusion drawn from the preceding two statements.<br><br>\r\nA. Healthy food is in great demand.	.<br>		B. Flax seeds and Horse gram are in great demand. .<br>\r\nC. Flax seed is in great demand. .<br>			D. Horse gram is in great demand. .<br>\r\nE. Flax seed and Horse gram are Healthy food.\r\n', 'CDA', 'AEB', 'EDC', 'BEA', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
