(2365, 218, 2, 'The number of factors of given number N is 39. What is the maximum number of distinct prime factors N can have?', '1', '2', '3', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2366, 218, 2, 'Four horses are tied on the four corners of a square of field of 20m length so that each horse can just touch the other two horses. They were able to graze in the area accessible to them for 22 days. For how many days is the un-grazed area sufficient for them?', '6 days', '4 days', '10 days	', '8 days', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2367, 218, 1, 'The unitâ€™s digit of a two-digit number is one more than the digit at tenâ€™s place. If the number is more than the five times of the sum of digits of the number, find the second highest number from all possible numbers', '59', '78', '67', '79', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2368, 218, 2, 'f(x)=log((1+x)/(1-x)) satisfies the equation', 'f(x + 2) â€“ 2f(x + 1) + f(x) = 0', 'f(x) â€“ f(x + 1) -  f(x(x + 1)) = 0', 'f(x1)  f(x2) =  f(x1 + x2)	', 'f(x<sub>1</sub> )+f(x<sub>2</sub>)=f((x<sub>1</sub>+x<sub>2</sub>)/(1+x<sub>1</sub> x<sub>2 </sub>))', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2369, 218, 2, 'A student was asked to find the sum of all the prime number between 10 and 40. He found the sum as 167. Which of the following statements is true?', 'He missed one prime number between 10 and 20', 'He missed one prime number between 20 and 30', 'He added one extra non-prime number between 10 and 20', 'None of these', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2370, 218, 2, '250 rupees is divided among four persons in such a way that when Rs. 4 is taken from the first person, Rs. 4 is given to the second person, the third personâ€™s share is divided by 4 and the fourth personâ€™s share is multiplied by 4, then all of them have the same amount. Which of the following statements is not correct?', 'The amount was divided in the ratio 12 : 8 : 5 : 20', 'At the end their combined money is Rs. 160', 'The combined share of first two persons is half that of the third person', 'None of these', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2371, 218, 1, 'The product of two odd functions is', 'always an even function		', 'Always an odd function', 'either even or odd function', 'not defined', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2376, 221, 2, 'Find the next term in the alpha-numerical series: Z1A, X2B, V6D, T21G, R88K, P445P,_____.', 'N2676V', 'V2676N', 'N2676U', 'U2670N', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2373, 221, 2, 'Five women: Nithya, Sanjana, Payal, Arpita, and Pallavi; and Five men: Farhan, Manav, Mayur, Arjun and Govind, sat on the two long sides of a rectangular table. Ladies sat alternating with and opposite to the men. Arjun sat in a centre position, Arpita sat opposite Farhan. Sanjana sat next to Arjun and three places from Farhan. Pallavi sat four places to the left of Arpita. Payal sat two places from Sanjana. Mayur sat opposite Sanjana. Manav sat three places from Pallavi. Who sat opposite to Nithya?', 'Farhan', 'Manav', 'Mayur	', 'Arjun', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2374, 221, 2, 'Five women: Urmila, Savithri, Primila, Aruna, and Pavithra; and Five men: Manoj, Arun, Kumar, Mahesh and Gopi, sat on the two long sides of a rectangular table. Ladies sat alternating with and opposite to the men. Arun sat three places from Pavithra. Savithri sat next to Mahesh and three places from Manoj. Pavithra sat four places to the left of Aruna. Primila sat two places from Savithri. Kumar sat opposite Savithri. Mahesh sat in a centre position, Aruna sat opposite Manoj. Who sat opposite to Gopi?', 'Savithri', 'Aruna', 'Pavithra	', 'Primila', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2375, 221, 2, 'In the series of letters, following some definite order, determine the next two letters in the correct order?\r\n	A, K, M, T, V, B, J, N, S, W, C, I, O, R, X, D, H, P, Q, Y, E, G, Q, ____ , ______ ', 'Y, Z	', 'P, Y	', 'Z, A	', 'P, Z', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2377, 220, 1, 'A player holds 17 cards of four suits of which nine are black and eight are red. There are twice as many diamonds as spades and thrice as many diamonds as hearts. How many clubs does he hold?', '4', '5', '6', '7', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2378, 220, 1, 'A box of dry fruits, worth Rs. 1000, weighs 200 g and contains Cashew, Badam and Pista. 20 g each of Cashew, Badam and Pista cost Rs. 5, Rs. 10 and Rs. 50 respectively. What is the quantity of Cashew (in grams) in the box?', '40', '80', '100', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2379, 220, 2, 'Imagine that your watch was correct at noon, but then it began to lose 20 minutes each hour. It now shows 5 pm, but it stopped 4.5 hours ago. What is the correct time now?', '11.30 pm', '12 noon', '1.00 am', '12 mid night', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2380, 221, 2, 'Find, the next group of three letters in the following series: ajs, fox, ___?__,  pyh, udm.', 'oxg', 'ktc	', 'bkt	', 'msy', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2381, 220, 2, 'Dhruv decides to solve a jigsaw puzzle made up of 330 pieces. He begins joining the pieces together to complete the puzzle. Each day he fits pieces together, he finds that there are fewer pieces left to be sorted out. As each day goes by, he is able to fit one more piece than the number of pieces he fit the previous day. On the first day he fits 25 pieces. How many days does it take him to complete the puzzle?', '12', '11', '10', '9', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2382, 220, 2, 'There are three flavours of candies â€“ Orange, Chocolate and Grape. There are twice as many Chocolate candies and Orange candies combined as there are Grape candies and twice as many Grape candies as there are Chocolate candies. Total number of candies is 144. How many of them are of Chocolate flavour?', '24', '28', '42', '56', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2383, 220, 1, 'If two labourers can build a house and a half in a day and a half, how many houses do nine labourers build in nine days, if they work at the same capacity?', '45', '9', '18', '40.5', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2384, 221, 2, 'An octagonal table is consecutively marked P to W at the corners in a clockwise manner. A Red cube is placed at P, while a Blue cube is placed at corner T. The Red cube moves one corner at a time clockwise, while the Blue cube moves anti-clockwise. The Blue cube first goes to the adjacent corner; then it misses one and goes to the next corner; then it misses two, then three, and so on. In how many moves and in which corner will the two cubes be together?', '4 moves, Corner S		', '5 moves, Corner T ', '7 moves, Corner U			', 'None of these.', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2385, 221, 2, 'What are the least number of weights required to measure weight in the range 1 to 40 kg?', '4', '5', '6', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2386, 220, 3, 'Shikha leaves office at 6.40 p.m. and catches a 7.00 p.m. local train that reaches Worli at 7.45 p.m. Her husband reaches the station to pick her up at 7.45 p.m. from the station as she gets off the train. Yesterday, Shikha left her office early and took a 6.10 p.m. train and arrived at 7.15 p.m. As her husband was not there to pick her up, she started walking towards their house. Her husband left their house at the usual time, saw his wife walking, turned around, picked her up and drove to their house 10 minutes earlier than usual. For how long did Shikha walk (in minutes) before her husband picked her up?', '10', '15', '20', '25', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2387, 221, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Refer the following data to answer the questions given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\nSeven language courses are offered by a certain arts college - Spanish, French, German, Hebrew, Mandarin, Sanskrit and Urdu. Students enrolling for a degree in arts should choose four languages in accordance with the following conditions. A student must do French if he opts for Spanish. Those who opt for Sanskrit must also do Urdu.  Urdu can''t be chosen by those who opt for German and Mandarin together. <br>\r\nWhich of the following can be selected by a student, if he doesn''t choose Spanish?<br>\r\na] Sanskrit<br>		b] French	<br>		c] Urdu<br>			d] German\r\n', 'only a and b	', 'a, b, c and d 	', 'only a, c and d	', 'only a and d', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2388, 221, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Refer the following data to answer the questions given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\nSeven language courses are offered by a certain arts college - Spanish, French, German, Hebrew, Mandarin, Sanskrit and Urdu. Students enrolling for a degree in arts should choose four languages in accordance with the following conditions. A student must do French if he opts for Spanish. Those who opt for Sanskrit must also do Urdu.  Urdu can''t be chosen by those who opt for German and Mandarin together. <br>\r\nWhich of the following subjects cannot be chosen, if Spanish and Hebrew are chosen? 	', 'Sanskrit', 'Urdu', 'French', 'German', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2389, 221, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Refer the following data to answer the questions given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\nSeven language courses are offered by a certain arts college - Spanish, French, German, Hebrew, Mandarin, Sanskrit and Urdu. Students enrolling for a degree in arts should choose four languages in accordance with the following conditions. A student must do French if he opts for Spanish. Those who opt for Sanskrit must also do Urdu.  Urdu can''t be chosen by those who opt for German and Mandarin together. <br>\r\n	Which of the following, invariably has to be chosen, if a student opts for Mandarin and German? \r\n', 'Sanskrit', 'Spanish', 'French', 'Hebrew', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2391, 220, 2, 'In a locality with 100 households, 24 buy Nandini milk, 25 buy Heritage milk and 32 buy Amul milk.  29 buy at least two of the three brands of milk and 3 buy all the three. If each house buying at least one brand of milk were to receive a poster of Rajinikanth, how many posters would be needed?', '78', '58', '48', '68', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2392, 220, 2, 'In a locality with 120 households, in the month of August, 2011, 24 buy Nandini milk, 25 buy Heritage milk and 32 buy Amul milk.  29 buy at least two of the three brands of milk and 3 buy all the three. Due to the intense marketing, in the month of September, 2011, if the Heritage milk captures 50% of the total untapped market, then what would be the number of households that buy Heritage milk in the month of September, 2011?', '50', '52', '54', '56', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2393, 220, 2, 'A bank offers 10% interest rate compounded annually. A person deposits Rs. 20,000 at the beginning of every year in his account. If he does not withdraw any amount, what would be the balance (in Rs.) in his account at the end of four years?', '102102', '90190', '29282', '102000', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2394, 223, 1, 'A, B, C, D, E and F are six persons who have to share three oranges and three apples in such a way that E takes an orange, A and D eat an apple each and C does not eat the same fruit as B and F. Who will eat the three oranges?', 'E, B and C	', 'F, B and D	', 'E, B and F	', 'E, C and F', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2395, 223, 1, 'Amit, Bina, Chotu, Dan and Elina are five friends with different heights. Amit is taller than Chotu but shorter than Elina, whereas, Bina is taller than Dan but not shorter than Elina. Who can be the tallest among the five?', 'Elina	', 'Amit', 'Bina		', 'Bina or Elina', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2396, 223, 1, 'Five friends A, B, C, D and E buy a book. They read the book one after the other. A is the last person to read the book. B or E can read the book only after D reads it. If E gives the book to B after reading, who reads the book after B and before A?', 'D', 'C', 'A', 'E', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2397, 223, 2, 'Four girls Padma, Queenie, Raji and Shweta learn four different forms of art - Singing, Dancing, Flute (Instrument) and Painting, not necessarily in that order. Each girl learns one form of art only. Padma does not learn dancing or Painting. Shweta cannot sing or play the flute. Which of the following girls can be in any of the classes?', 'Only Raji	', 'Only Queenie	', 'Only Shweta	', 'Both Queenie and Raji', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2398, 223, 1, 'In a Blue Cross organisation, seven animals (two dogs A and B, two cats C and D, and three rabbits E, F and G) are made to sit in a row, in order to vaccinate. Exactly one animal (a dog) sits in between C and D. A alone sits in between G and E. No two animals of the same species sit next to each other. E sits to the immediate left of C. Who sits at the extreme left of the row?', 'G', 'E', 'F', 'C', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2399, 223, 1, 'Two Indians, three Americans and two Africans attended an interview in which five of them are selected. If only one Indian and two Americans are selected, then which of the following is definitely true?', 'The total number of ways of selecting the five people is eight', 'The two Africans are sure to get selected.', 'Only one African is selected', 'More than one of the above', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2400, 222, 3, 'Lalitha distributes a few one-rupee coins, a few two-rupee coins and four five-rupee coins to three of her students. The total amount that each boy receives is the same. What is the minimum number of coins that were distributed by Lalitha?', '6', '7', '9', '10', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2401, 223, 2, 'Eight friends are sitting on a circular table. Madan, Neel, Omar and Preeti sit in the directions of North, East, South and West (not necessarily in the same order). Ashwini, Bindu, Chatur and Dave sit in the directions of North-east, North-west, South-east and South-west (not necessarily in the same order). Ashwini sits in between Madan and Neel, who are not sitting opposite each other. Bindu and Dave sit in opposite directions. Preeti sits to the left of Neel. Which of the following pairs of friends do not sit opposite each other?', 'Ashwini and Chatur 	', 'Bindu and Dave ', 'Madan and Preeti	', 'Madan and Omar ', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2402, 223, 1, 'Three persons A, B and C visit three restaurants P, Q and R for break-fast, lunch and dinner on a certain day. Each person visits all three restaurants. No two persons can go to the same restaurant for the same meal of the day. If B visits Q for break-fast and C goes to P for dinner, then which of the following must be TRUE?', 'A goes to Q for break-fast	', 'C goes to Q for dinner', 'A goes to R for lunch', 'A goes to P for lunch', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2403, 223, 2, 'Kunal, Varsha, Raunak, Karuna and Sowmya have five cycles of five different colours - Blue, White, Red, Orange and Green. The Green cycle is the smallest of all the cycles and Karuna owns it. Sowmyaâ€™s cycle is neither Blue nor White and is taller than the cycles owned by Varsha and Raunak. One person''s name starts with the same letter as the first letter of the cycleâ€™s colour and it is the second biggest of all. Which of the following is TRUE about the owner of the cycle, its colour and its height?', 'Sowmya - Blue â€“ Smallest	', 'Varsha - Red - Biggest', 'Sowmya - Orange â€“ Biggest', 'Karuna - Green - Biggest', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2404, 223, 2, 'Each of the three girls gets at least one hairband out of 6 hairbands, at least one hairclip out of 6 hairclips and at least one chocolate out of 6 chocolates, such that the total number of the items that each of them gets is the same. No one gets the same number of hairclips, hairbands and chocolates. Then which of the following is TRUE?', 'Each girl gets 2 hairclips, 2 hairbands and 2 chocolates', 'Each girl gets 2 hairclips and 2 hairbands', 'Each girl gets 1 hairband, 2 chocolates and 3 hairclips', 'The number of hairclips, hairbands and chocolates that each girl gets is 1, 2 and 3 not necessarily in that order', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2405, 223, 2, 'P and Q play Violin, whereas R and S play Flute. T and U play Guitar, but V and W play saxophone. Having won their respective competitions, they sit in a row for a photograph session. T sits to the immediate right of W and P sits at an extreme end. A Violin player is at the fourth place from the left end of the row. W and T do not sit between R and U. Which of the following pairs of persons have exactly two persons seated between them, while no one sits to the left of R. The number of persons seated between P and U is same as the number of persons seated between R and T.', 'R and W	', 'S and V 		', 'U and T	', 'R and Q', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2406, 223, 2, 'Five friends P, Q, R, S and T forward letters among themselves in the following manner:  P sends letters to Q, S and T. T sends letters to R, while P and R exchange letters with each other. Q sends letters to S, who sends letters to T. If P has to forward his letters to R, in how many ways can the letters be forwarded?', 'Two	', 'Three ', 'Four', 'One', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2407, 223, 1, 'A, B, C, D, P, Q, R, and S are eight students who are part of either the cricket team or the football team of their college (four in each). P and Q are not in the same team. A and B are in different teams. B is in the same team as that of R and S. Who else is a part of the team with B, R and S?', 'P	', 'Q	', 'P or Q	', 'A or C', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2408, 223, 2, 'Five boys Vijay, Harish, Manu, Lalit and Roshan compete in a 100 m race. Manu runs faster than Roshan and Lalit is slower than Vijay. Harish runs faster than Lalit and Roshan. Who among the following is definitely not the winner?', 'Vijay', 'Harish	', 'Manu	', 'Lalit', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2409, 223, 2, 'There are three boxes of three different colours - Orange. Black and Purple and 6 shirts - 2 Orange,  2 Black and 2 Purple. The shirts are packed in the three boxes such that each box has 2 shirts of different colours and also the colour of the box is different from the colour of the shirts packed in it.  10 chocolates are kept in these boxes in such a way that the Orange box has the maximum possible chocolates in it, whereas the Purple box has the least possible chocolates in it. Each box should have at least one chocolate and no two boxes have the same number of chocolates. Which of the following is true?', 'The Orange box, the Black box and the Purple box have 6, 3 and 1 chocolates in them respectively', 'The box which has the shirts of Purple and Black colours has 8 chocolates in it.', 'The box which has the shirts of Black and Orange colours has 3 chocolates in it.', 'The box which has the shirts of Orange and Purple colours has 2 chocolates in it.', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2410, 223, 3, 'Five drinks P, Q, R, S and T are of five different colours among red, green, blue, yellow, white and orange. P is of green colour and T is not of red colour. Q is costlier than the drink which is of green colour and cheaper than the drink which is of yellow colour whereas, yellow coloured drink is cheaper than the white coloured drink. S is of white colour and T is the costliest drink. Which of the following must be FALSE?', 'The colour of Q is red or blue or orange.', 'The cheapest drink is P.', 'The colour of T is yellow.', 'R is costlier than P.  ', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2411, 223, 2, 'P, Q, R, S and T are five corners of pentagon. Five books A, B, C, D and E are placed along the sides joining the angular corners. Neither P, Q, R, S and T nor A, B, C, D and E are necessarily in that order. Book A is on the side joining the corners P and R. S is to the immediate right of P, and R is in between P and T. B is on the side joining Q and T. D and E are on either side of B. C is placed on the side joining the corners ', 'P and R	', 'S and Q	', 'S and T	', 'P and S', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2412, 223, 2, 'A telephone network between six flats A, B, C, D, E and F is as follows:  The pairs of houses - AE, AD, EB, BC, EC, BF, FD â€“ are connected. All the connecting links are two-ways.  How many pairs of flats more have to be connected, so that every pair of A, B, C, D, E, F is connected?', '7', '6', '5', 'None of these', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2413, 223, 2, 'Priyanka Khanna wears shoes and carries hand bags of different colours on five days of a week from Monday to Friday. Each pair of shoes is of exactly one colour - Blue, White, Yellow, Red and Green. The five bags are of five different colours - Orange, Maroon, Black, Silver and Blue. She wears a pair of shoes and carries a hand bag of the same colour on one of the five days. The combination of Green shoes and Black bag is used on Tuesday. White and Orange combination is used on Friday. Red and Silver is not one of her combinations and she wears Red shoes on Thursday. The Silver bag is used on Wednesday. She must be wearing the Blue shoes on ', 'Wednesday	', 'Monday	', 'Thursday	', 'Sunday\r\n', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2414, 225, 2, 'Manoj, Vinod, Prajwal, Farhan, Krish are five boys in a class whose running speeds and weights are compared. It is found that Manoj holds the same place in the decreasing orders of running speeds and weights of the five boys. Farhan is heavier than Vinod and faster than Prajwal. Vinod is the fastest of all but lighter than Prajwal. Krish is faster than Farhan but slower than Manoj. Which of the following is definitely FALSE?', 'Krish is lighter than Vinod', 'Prajwal is faster than Farhan', 'Manoj is second in the decreasing orders of weights and running speeds', 'Vinod is the only person faster than Manoj', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2415, 225, 1, 'Five pastries â€“ Black-forest, Chocolate Fantasy, Irish Coffee, Pineapple and Blueberry - are packed in five boxes, which are kept from left to right in a row. It is found that the Black-forestâ€™s box is to the left of the Blueberry''s box, which is to the immediate left of the Chocolate Fantasyâ€™s box. Irish Coffeeâ€™s box is kept at the extreme left and there is one box between that and the Black-forestâ€™s box. Which itemâ€™s box is to the immediate right of the Black-forestâ€™s box?', 'Pineapple	', 'Blueberry		', 'Chocolate Fantasy', 'Irish Coffee', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2416, 225, 1, 'A rectangular table has one chair each on its smaller sides and two chairs each on its longer sides. Six persons Gargi, Samantha, Carol, Divya, Esha and Smitha sit on the six spaced chairs around the table for a board meeting. Samantha sits to the immediate left of Divya and opposite Esha. Carol and Smitha sit opposite to each other and Divya is alone on one of the sides. Who sits opposite to Divya?', 'Gargi', 'Samantha	', 'Esha', 'Carol', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2417, 225, 1, 'A wine taster has to taste five bottles of wine A, B, C, D and E. If he tastes B, he cannot taste C immediately. If he tastes A, he cannot taste E after that. Which of the following can be the correct order in which tastes the wines? ', 'A, B, C, D, E', 'D, B, C, E, A', 'D, C, B, A, E ', 'D, C, B, E, A', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2418, 225, 2, 'Parul, Queenie, Rita, Shradha, Tina, Urvashi and Veena are seven singers of a group. Rita is louder than only four of them. Parul is not as loud as Queenie, but louder than Tina, who is louder than Urvashi but not as loud as Veena. Queenie, who is not as loud as Shraddha, is louder than Veena. Who is the loudest of all? ', 'Parul ', 'Queenie	', 'Shradha		', 'Rita', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2419, 225, 3, 'Three friends bought books of different genres among Romance, Thriller, Philosophy, Self-help, Business, Children, Travel, Biographies and Health. Each person buys three books of different genres. A Philosophy book was bought by the person who bought a Children''s book. Books on Romance and Biographies were bought by different persons and neither of these was bought by the person who bought a Travel book. A Health book and a Biography book were bought by the same person and a Romance book was bought by the person who bought a Business book. Which of the following cannot be a set of three books which were bought by one of the three friends?', 'Thriller, Romance and Business	', 'Health, Biography and Self-help', 'Children, Travel and Philosophy		', 'Thriller, Self-help and Business', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2420, 225, 2, 'Five persons â€“ Avinash, Bhoomika, Chirag, Daniel and Esha own five different cars â€“ Alto, Santro, Zen, i10 and Swift. Neither Esha nor Bhoomika own an Alto. Avinash and Daniel own Santro and Zen, in any order. Who owns the Alto?', 'Avinash	', 'Bhoomika		', 'Chirag	', 'Daniel', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2421, 225, 2, 'Anusha, Barkha, Chitra, Devika, Elina and Faria sit around a circular table in six chairs. Anusha sits opposite to Devika. Chitra is to the immediate right of Anusha and is next to Elina. Which of the following is definitely FALSE?', 'Anusha and Elina are not opposite each other', 'Elina is between Chitra and Devika', 'Chitra is in between Anusha and Elina	', 'Barkha and Faria are opposite to each other', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2422, 224, 1, 'A, B, C, D and E are five cities. Each pair of cities has a path connecting them. How many paths are there in all? ', '12', '10', '5', '2', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2423, 225, 2, 'Susheela, Viren and Karthik meet at Delhi. Each of them belongs to different cities among Chennai, Bangalore and Mumbai. Susheela is not from Bangalore or Chennai. If Karthik is from Bangalore, then Viren is NOT from', 'Mumbai or Bangalore	', 'Mumbai or Chennai', 'Chennai or Bangalore', 'Chennai or Mumbai or Bangalore', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2424, 225, 2, 'An Indian, an American, an Australian, a Jamaican and a European are seated in a row. The Indian do not wish to sit immediately next to the European or the Jamaican. The European and the Jamaican sit immediately next to each other. The Australian is at the extreme right end of the row. The Indian is immediately to the left of the Australian. Who is seated in the middle of the row? ', 'Jamaican		', 'Indian', 'European	', 'American', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2425, 225, 2, 'Five dogs Alsatian, Bulldog, Cocker Spaniel, German Shepherd and Pomeranian are in a row. Cocker Spaniel sits to the immediate right of Pomeranian. If Alsatian and Bulldog have only two dogs sitting between them, which of the following must be true?', 'Alsatian is at an extreme end of the row', 'Bulldog is sitting beside Alsatian', 'Pomeranian or Cocker Spaniel must be at one extreme end of the row', 'German Shepherd must be at one of the ends of the row', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2426, 225, 2, 'Four boys P, Q, R and S; three girls A, B and C are standing in a row, facing North. Girl C has as many people to her left as to her right. None of the boys is at either of the extreme ends of the row. Boy P is standing to the immediate right of girl A, while girl C is standing to the immediate left of boy R. Who is standing fourth from the right end of the queue?', 'C', 'S', 'R', 'A', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2427, 225, 2, 'Eight persons Anvesha, Babita, Charita, Dolly, Parineeta, Qadira, Raveena and Sahitya sit in two teams with four in each team facing each other. Anvesha and Babita are not in the same team. Parineeta sits to the immediate left of Charita in the same team but opposite to Qadira. Raveena and Babita have only two persons between them. Anvesha and Parineeta have only one person between them. Which of these pairs of persons can sit diagonally opposite to each other?', 'Sahitya and Dolly or Qadira and Raveena	', 'Parineeta and Anvesha or Anvesha and Charita', 'Anvesha and Babita or Raveena and Charita	', 'Either [1] or [2]', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2428, 225, 1, 'Five single-movie DVDs - DDLJ, Black, RaOne, Dhoom II and K3G are arranged in a shelf, one above the other. RaOne DVD is neither on top nor at the bottom. Black DVD and K3G  DVD have exactly two DVDs between them, same as RaOne and DDLJ  DVDs. Which of the following movie DVDs has to be in the middle of the shelf?', 'RaOne 	', 'DDLJ', 'Dhoom II 	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2429, 225, 3, 'Scarves of six colours - Orange, Purple, Black, Green, Blue and Pink - are sold at a shop. Three girls â€“ Vinutha, Krithika and Shikha - go to the shop to buy scarves. Each girl buys only two scarves of different colours. All the scarves are single coloured. The scarves bought by each girl are different in colour from those of the other two girls. Green and Purple scarves are bought by one girl. Shikha has a Black scarf, whereas Pink and Orange scarves are not bought by the same girl. If Vinuthaâ€™s scarves are neither Pink nor Blue in colour, then the colours of Vinutha''s scarves are', 'Green and Purple		', 'Blue and Orange', 'Orange and Black', 'Pink and Green', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2430, 225, 1, 'A, B, C and D are four friends. Each owns one of the following â€“ a Flat, a Car, a Macbook and a Blackberry - not necessarily in that order. A and C do not own a flat, whereas B and C do not own a Blackberry. If B has a car, whereas  D and A cannot afford a Macbook then which of the following must be the owner of the flat?', 'C', 'A', 'D', 'Either C or D ', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2431, 225, 2, 'X, Y and Z are the three drivers and P, Q and R are three conductors in BMTC. Each of the three buses â€“ 201G, 201R and 201M requires a driver and a conductor. Y is not in 201G and R is always on 201R. X does not come in 201R and Q is in 201M. P and X always work together. Which of the following is definitely a proper combination of driver, conductor and the bus number? ', 'P, X â€“ 201G', 'Z, R â€“ 201R 	', 'Y, Q â€“ 201M 	', 'Z, Q â€“ 201M', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2432, 225, 3, 'Sandeep, Pranav and Ankit are three boys who choose two subjects each out of 6 subjects Physics, Chemistry, Maths, Electronics, Computers and Biology. Pranav chooses neither Chemistry nor Biology and these two subjects are not chosen by the same person. Ankit chooses Maths. Which of the following additional information will fix the distribution properly?', 'Pranav chooses Physics and Electronics', 'Ankit chooses Biology', 'Sandeep chooses Chemistry and Electronics', 'Ankit chooses Computers and Electronics ', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2433, 225, 2, 'Five temples A, B, C, D and E are located in five cities P, Q, R, S and T, but not necessarily in the same order. No two temples are in the same city. B is neither in R nor in T. A is neither in P nor in Q. C is neither in T nor in R. D is in R while P has C in it. Which of the following is definitely FALSE?', 'If B is in S, then A is in T		', 'If S has B, then E must be in T', 'If A is in S, then E must be in T	', 'A may be in S or T ', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2434, 227, 1, 'K, L, M, N, O and P are buildings in Bangalore. Neither M nor N is the tallest building. L is taller than P but shorter than K. O is not as tall as P, but taller than M. Which of the following buildings is the tallest?', 'O', 'M', 'K', 'L', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2435, 227, 1, 'When the reports of the annual income of five families (A, B, C, D, and E) were submitted, it was found that no two families had the same income. Bâ€™s income is more than that of D but less than that of E, whereas Aâ€™s income is more than Câ€™s income but less than Eâ€™s income. Which of the following families has got the highest income?', 'A', 'E', 'B', 'D', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2436, 227, 1, 'Six employees A, B, C, D, E and F arrive at their office in such a way that C arrives before F and after D, whereas E arrives before B, who arrives before F.  A arrives after both F and C arrive. Who is the last person to arrive?', 'B', 'A', 'C', 'D', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2437, 227, 2, 'A train has seven coaches viz. P, Q, R, S, T, U and V. The coach R is the third from the last and the coach V is the second from the engine. The coach Q and the coach U have exactly three coaches in between. Either S or P is the only coach between R and U. The coach right behind the engine is', 'T or S or Q	', 'T or R or V	', 'T or S or P		', 'T or S or R', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2438, 227, 3, 'There are five shelves of five different colours - Black, White, Blue, Brown and Red. Each of them is of a different weight and of a different cost and are numbered from 1 to 5 from the heaviest to the lightest and the costliest to the cheapest. The Blue shelf is the 4th in the order of weights and costlier than the Red shelf, whereas the Brown shelf is the lightest of all. The Red shelf is lighter than the White shelf and heavier than the Black shelf, which is the cheapest of all. Which of these is the heaviest of all shelves?', 'Black ', 'White 	', 'Brown       		', 'Blue ', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2439, 227, 1, 'Eight friends A, B, C, D, E, F, G and H go on a picnic in two batches of four each. Neither A and C nor D and F go together. B and H have to go together. If B and C go in one batch, then which of the following can be in the other batch?', 'A, D, F and G', 'A, D, E and G ', 'A, D, E and F	', 'A, C, E and G', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2440, 227, 2, 'Three marketing executives - Sheila Samaira and Monica have to choose three cities each, out of the six cities â€“ New York, California, Paris, Singapore, Sydney and Dubai, to market a beauty care product. If Dubai is chosen, then New York cannot be chosen by the same person. If Monica chooses Paris, then Sheila does not choose Dubai. If Samaira chooses California, then Monica cannot choose Paris and if Sheila chooses New York, then Monica chooses Sydney and Dubai. If Monica chooses Dubai and Samaira chooses California, then Monica cannot choose', 'New York and Paris', 'California and Paris', 'Paris and Singapore	', 'New York and Sydney', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2441, 227, 2, 'Kavita, Archana, Mohit, Jairam, Seema and Manish are six students, out of whom three are to be selected for a quiz competition. If Archana is selected, then neither Jairam nor Kavita is selected. If Seema is selected, then Kavita must be selected, but Manish cannot be selected. If Archana is selected, then who must be selected?', 'Seema and Mohit	', 'Kavita and Manish', 'Mohit and Manish	', 'Either [1] or [3]', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2442, 227, 2, 'M, N, O, P, Q, R, S, T and U are nine tennis players who are shortlisted by Indian Tennis Federation to be coached by Leander Paes or Mahesh Bhupathi. Both Paes and Bhupathi have time to coach only three players. P is the best among the nine and both Paes and Bhupathi show interest in him. R and N do not wish to be coached by either Paes or Bhupati. S is picked by Paes and T by Bhupathi. O comes back saying that neither of the two coaches selected him. M and P; U and Q are not coached by the same coach. Which of the following is a possible combination of the coach and the players coached by him?', 'Bhupati -  T, U, P 		', 'Paes - S, R, U', 'Bhupati  - T, N, U', 'Paes - P , S, M', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2443, 227, 1, 'Four out of seven employees A, B, C, D, E, F and G are to be selected to represent the company in a world conference in such a way that if A is selected, then B cannot be among the four and if B is selected, then E cannot be among the four. If one of D and F is selected, then the other must be chosen. Which of the following statements must be true?', 'If B is selected, then D must be selected	', 'If A is selected, then C must be selected', 'If B is selected, then G must be selected', 'C must be selected', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2444, 227, 1, 'Five friends Vijay, Ganga, Astha, Sanjeev and Tanya sit around a table. Tanya is to the immediate right of Vijay. Ganga and Astha are on either sides of Sanjeev. Who sits between Astha and Tanya, assuming that there is only one person between them?', 'Ganga', 'Vijay	', 'Sanjeev	', 'Ganga or Sanjeev', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2445, 227, 2, 'A, B, C. D and E are five chairs placed round a pentagonal table to seat Pooja, Quaza, Raima, Salma and Tamanna, who participate in a conference. E is placed between B and A. D is placed to the immediate left of B. Pooja is in chair C with Raima and Quaza on either sides of her. Tamanna is to the immediate right of Quaza. Which of the following is a FALSE statement?', 'Quaza is in chair D		', 'Salma is in chair E', 'Raima is not in chair A', 'Tamanna is adjacent to Salma', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2446, 227, 3, 'Six men - M, N, O, P, Q, R and six women â€“ A, B, C, D, E, F are seated at six tables, placed in the hexagonal form. All the persons are facing towards the centre of the hexagon. Six couples-(M, A), (N, B), (O, C), (P, D), (Q, E) and (R, F) are accommodated at tables (two per table). The couple (M, A) sits opposite to the couple (R, F). R sits to the immediate left of B. Q sits to the immediate right of A. The three persons seated between M and P are', 'A, Q, E', 'Q, E, D', 'A, O, C		', 'O, C, N', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2447, 227, 2, 'Prasanna, Shiva, Gopal, Altaf, Sahil and David are captains of state-level cricket teams. They attend a meeting before the Ranji tournament and sit around a hexagonal table. They wear uniforms of six different colours - Grey, Green, Red, Black, Maroon and Yellow. David and Sahil sit opposite each other. Sahil sits to the immediate left of the person, who is in Green uniform and David sits to the immediate right of the person in Red uniform. Prasanna sits to the immediate right of David. Gopal is in Green uniform and Sahil wears the Yellow uniform. The person in Red uniform is not next to the person in Grey uniform, but sits opposite to the person who is in Maroon uniform. Which of the following statements is FALSE?', 'Altaf and Shiva do not sit opposite to each other', 'Persons wearing Yellow and Grey uniforms are not opposite each other', 'Prasanna does not wear a Black uniform and is not next to Gopal', 'Altaf wears either a Red or a Maroon uniform', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2448, 227, 3, '	Four girls - A, B, C and D form an inner circle and four boys - P, Q, R and S form the outer circle. Each of them faces towards the centre.  When looked from the centre, each of the boys seems to be standing on the inner circle in between two girls, standing adjacent to each other. P and Q; R and S;     A and D; B and C are opposite each other. Which of the following information is helpful to determine the arrangement of the boys and girls completely?', 'R is to the right of Q and between A and C.', 'P lies between A and B.', 'P, R, Q and S stand in clockwise order', 'S is to the right of P and D is to the left of C between P and R', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2449, 227, 2, 'Abhijeet has to visit five cities P, Q, R, S and T. He visits the cities under some constraints. He can directly go to P and then to S. He can directly go to Q and then to T. He can directly go to R and then to P or Q. Which of the following statements is definitely TRUE? ', 'Abhijeet cannot visit all the cities without visiting at least one city twice.', 'Abhijeet can reach all of them without touching any of them twice.', 'Abhijeet must touch R to go to S.', 'Abhijeet must touch R to go to Q.', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2450, 227, 2, 'Among the five major cities - Pune, Kolkata, Bangalore, Chennai and Mumbai, all the cities, except Pune, have direct flights from Delhi. Mumbai and Chennai are interconnected by two way flights, and so are Chennai and Kolkata.  Pune can be reached only from Bangalore or Kolkata. There are no other interconnected routes.  If one wishes to go to Pune from Chennai, without touching Delhi, he has to pass through', 'Kolkata', 'Mumbai or Bangalore', 'Bangalore              ', 'Mumbai', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2451, 227, 2, 'P â€“ a school, Q â€“ a restaurant, R â€“ a hospital and S â€“ a park are connected along the sides of a square and also connected diagonally. P, Q, R, S are in clockwise order. Varunâ€™s home, T, is at the intersection of the roads PR and QS. In how many ways can Varun start from T and go to all four places, without visiting any of the places twice?', '4', '12', '16', '8', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2452, 227, 2, 'A, B, C, D, E and F are six persons who have to be given three fruits and three sweets. E is given a fruit. Each of A and D gets a sweet and C does not get the same type of eatable as B and F get. Who will get the fruits?', 'E, B and C', 'F, B and D		', 'E, B and F		', 'E, C and F ', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2453, 227, 3, 'The five cities A, B, C, D and E are connected as follows: four two-way roads between A and B,  two one-way roads from B to C, three two-way roads between B and D, only a one-way road from B to E, a two-way road between C and D and two one-way roads from D to E. The maximum possible ways for a car to go from D to A, without touching E, is ', '20', '16', '14', '12', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2454, 229, 3, 'In a city, there are two types of people â€“ Honesties and Swindlers. Honesties always speak the truth and Swindlers always speak lies. One day, I met three people Alpha, Beta and Gamma of the city, and asked them ''Who among you is the truth teller?"<br>\r\nThe following were their replies: <br>\r\nAlpha: I am not a Swindler.	<br>\r\nBeta: Gama is not a Swindler. <br>\r\nGamma: Beta is Honesty. <br>\r\nIf it was known that exactly one person among the three was Honesty and the other two were Swindlers, then who among them must be the Honesty?\r\n', 'Alpha', 'Beta	', 'Gamma	', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2455, 229, 3, 'One day, I met three persons Alpha, Beta and Gamma, each of whom belonged to a different tribe amongst Honesters, Swindlers and Ambivators. It is also known that the Honesters always speak the truth, the Swindlers always speak lies and the Ambivators alternate between the truth and lies, in any order. When they are asked to introduce themselves, each of them gave two replies as given below. <br>\r\nAlpha: Beta is the Swindler. I am the Honester. <br>\r\nBeta: I am not the Swindler. Gamma is the Honester. <br>\r\nGamma: Alpha is not the Honester. I am not the Swindler. <br>\r\nWho among the three persons is a Swindler?\r\n', 'Alpha	', 'Beta	', 'Gamma	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2456, 229, 3, 'Police arrested three persons - Chotu, Motu and Gotu - on suspicion, in a theft case. It was found that one among these three was the thief. During the interrogation, their replies were as follows:\r\nChotu: I am not the thief. Either Motu or Gotu is the thief. <br>\r\nMotu: I am not the thief. Chotu is the thief. <br>\r\nGotu: I am not the thief. Motu is the thief. <br>\r\nIf exactly one person among them always speaks the truth, another always speaks lies and the third alternates between the truth and lies, in any order, then who is the thief?\r\n', 'Chotu', 'Gotu', 'Motu', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `qb_options` (`id`, `cat_id`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `answer1`, `answer2`, `answer3`, `answer4`, `answer5`, `option1`, `option2`, `option3`, `option4`, `option5`, `status`) VALUES
(2457, 229, 3, 'Three friends â€“ Amit, Bittu and Chintu were of different heights. When asked â€œWho among the three of you is the tallest?â€ the following were their replies: <br>\r\nAmit: I am the tallest. Bittu is not the tallest<br>\r\nBittu: I am the tallest. Amit is shortest<br>\r\nChintu: I am the tallest. Bittu is the shortest. <br>\r\nIt is known that one among them always tells the truth, one always speaks lies and one alternates between the truth and lies (not necessarily in the same order). Who can never be the tallest? \r\n', 'Amit	', 'Bittu		', 'Chintu	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2458, 229, 3, 'Three athletes- Anand, Bharat and Charan - participated in a long jump event and each one of them won exactly one medal among Gold, Silver and Bronze. Exactly one among them always speaks the truth, another always speaks lies and the last person always alternates between the truth and a lie (in any order). When asked about the medals each of them won, the following were their replies:\r\nAnand: Bharat won Gold. I won Bronze. <br>\r\nBharat: Charan won Silver. Anand did not win Gold. <br>\r\nCharan: Bharat won Bronze. Anand did not win Silver. <br>\r\nWho won the Gold, Bronze and Silver respectively? <br>\r\n', 'Anand, Bharat, Charan	', 'Bharat, Charan, Anand	', 'Charan, Anand, Bharat			', 'Anand, Charan, Bharat', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2459, 229, 3, 'In a class, three students - Vijay, Bhaskar and Kumar- are the top three rankers, i.e. 1st, 2nd and 3rd and in any order. Each student among them gives two replies to any question, one of which is true and the other is false (in any order). When asked about the ranks they got, the following were their replies. <br>\r\nBhaskar: I got the first rank. Vijay got the second rank. <br>\r\nKumar: I got the first rank. Bhaskar got the second rank. <br>\r\nVijay: I got the first rank. Bhaskar got the third rank. <br>\r\nWhich among the following is the correct order of the persons who got the first, the second and the third ranks respectively?\r\n', 'Vijay, Bhaskar, Kumar	', 'Kumar, Bhaskar, Vijay		', 'Kumar, Vijay, Bhaskar		', 'Bhaskar, Kumar, Vijay', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2460, 229, 3, 'Each of Suresh, Ramesh and Dinesh is the professor of a different subject among - History, Geography and Economics, not necessarily in the same order. When asked about their subjects, each professor gives two replies to any question asked to them, at least one of which is true. There is exactly one professor who always speaks the truth. The following were their replies:\r\nSuresh: I am a History professor. Dinesh is the Geography professor \r\nDinesh: I am an Economics professor. Suresh is the Geography professor \r\nRamesh: I am not a History professor. Suresh is the Economics professor\r\nWhich among the following is the correct order of the professors of History, Geography and Economics respectively?\r\n', 'Suresh, Ramesh, Dinesh	', 'Ramesh, Dinesh, Suresh		', 'Suresh, Dinesh, Ramesh', 'Data Inconsistent', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2461, 229, 3, 'Each of the three friends - Sahana, Vandana and Shobana- plays exactly one instrument among Violin, Veena and Guitar, not necessarily in the same order. Each girl always gives two replies to any question. Out of these three friends, exactly one girl always speaks the truth, one always lies and one always alternates between the truth and lies, in any order. When each was asked â€œWhich game do you play?â€, the following were their replies: <br>\r\nSahana: I am a Violin player. Vandana is a Veena player. <br>\r\nVandana: I am a Violin player. Shobana is a Guitar player. <br>\r\nShobana: Sahana is a Veena player. Vandana is a Violin player. <br>\r\nWho among the three friends is a liar? 	\r\n', 'Sahana	', 'Vandana', 'Shobana 		', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2462, 229, 3, 'Each of the three players - Arun, Varun and Tarun- plays exactly one game among Cricket, Football and Golf, not necessarily in the same order. Each player always gives two replies to any question. Out of these three players, exactly one player always speaks the truth, one always lies and one always alternates between the truth and lies, in any order. When each was asked â€œWhich game do you play?â€, the following were their replies: <br>\r\nArun: I play Cricket. Varun is a Football player. <br>\r\nVarun: I play Cricket. Tarun is a Golf player. <br>\r\nTarun: Arun is a Football player. Varun is a Cricketer. <br>\r\n	Who among the three players must be the Golf player? <br>\r\n', 'Arun	', 'Varun	', 'Tarun 		', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2463, 229, 3, 'Each of the three players - Karan, Kiran and Karun- plays exactly one game among Kabaddi, Snooker and Bowling, not necessarily in the same order. Each player always gives two replies to any question. Out of these three players, exactly one player always speaks the truth, one always lies and one always alternates between the truth and lies, in any order. When each was asked â€œWhich game do you play?â€, the following were their replies: <br>\r\nKaran: I play Kabaddi. Kiran is a Snooker player. <br>\r\nKiran: I play Kabaddi. Karun is a Bowling player. <br>\r\nKarun: Karan is a Snooker player. Kiran is a Kabaddi player. <br>\r\nWhich game does Kiran play? \r\n', 'Kabaddi	', 'Snooker	', 'Bowling 	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2464, 229, 3, 'Each of the three friends - Ayesha, Barkha and Carol - has a different profession among -Doctor, Lawyer and Singer - not necessarily in the same order. It was known that each of them spoke at least one true statement. When asked â€œWho belongs to which profession?â€, the following were their replies: <br>\r\nAyesha: Carol is the Singer. Barkha is the Lawyer. <br>\r\nBarkha: Ayesha is the Doctor. Carol is not the Lawyer. <br> \r\nCarol: Barkha is the Lawyer. I am the Doctor. <br>\r\nWho is the Lawyer?\r\n', 'Ayesha	', 'Carol', 'Barkha		', 'Indeterminate\r\n', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2465, 229, 3, 'Each of the three friends - Vidya, Nitya and Satya has a different profession among - Software Engineer, Journalist and Chartered Accountant - not necessarily in the same order. It was known that each of them spoke at least one true statement. When asked â€œWho belongs to which profession?â€, the following were their replies : <br>\r\nVidya: Satya is the Chartered Accountant. Nitya is the Journalist. <br>\r\nNitya: Vidya is the Software Engineer. Satya is not the Journalist. <br>\r\nSatya: Nitya is the Journalist. I am the Software Engineer. <br>\r\nWhat is Vidya''s profession?\r\n', 'Software Engineer', 'Journalist		', 'Chartered Accountant	', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2466, 229, 3, 'Each of the three friends - Amrutha, Vaishali and Sushma has a different profession among -Teacher, Trainer and Athlete - not necessarily in the same order. It was known that each of them spoke at least one true statement. When asked â€œWho belongs to which profession?â€, the following were their replies : <br>\r\nAmrutha: Sushma is the Athlete. Vaishali is the Trainer. <br>\r\nVaishali: Amrutha is the Teacher. Sushma is the Trainer. <br>\r\nSushma: Vaishali is the Trainer. I am the Teacher. <br>\r\nAmong the three, who speaks the truth, always?\r\n', 'Amrutha	', 'Vaishali	', 'Sushma		', 'Indeterminate\r\n', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2467, 229, 3, 'In a cricket match, the total number of runs scored by Kunal, Dilip and Rajesh together is 120. When asked about the individual runs scored by them, following were their replies.\r\nKunal: I scored 40 runs. Rajesh is not the least scorer. <br>\r\nDilip: Kunal scored the maximum number of runs. I scored the minimum number of runs. <br>\r\nRajesh: Kunal scored the minimum number of runs. Dilip scored 40 runs. <br>\r\nIt was also known that one among them always speak the truth, another player always lies and the third player alternates between the truth and lies, in any order.  <br>\r\n	If each of them scored equal number of runs, then who among them always lies?\r\n', 'Kunal', 'Dilip', 'Rajesh	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2468, 229, 3, 'In a basketball match, the total number of baskets scored by John, Ben and David together is 12. When asked about the individual baskets scored by them, the following were their replies. <br>\r\nJohn: I scored 4 baskets. David is not the least scorer. <br>\r\nBen: John scored the maximum number of baskets. I scored the minimum number of baskets. <br>\r\nDavid: John scored the minimum number of baskets. Ben scored 4 baskets. <br>\r\nEach player scored at least one basket. It was also known that one player among them always speak the truth, another player always lies and the third player alternates between the truth and lies, in any order. If the baskets scored by the three players are 3, 4 and 5 (not necessarily in the same order), then which player scored 5 baskets?\r\n', 'Ben	', 'John	', 'David		', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2469, 229, 2, 'One among three students - Anna, Mona and Sona - is the fastest runner in the class. Each one of them claims to be the fastest. It was also known that among them, there is one student who always speaks the truth, one who always speaks lies and another whose statement cannot be considered as either true or false. The following are the statements made by them. <br>\r\nAnna: I am not a Liar. <br>\r\nMona: I am the Liar. <br>\r\nSona: I neither speak the truth nor do I speak lies. <br>\r\nWho is the fastest runner?\r\n', 'Anna', 'Mona', 'Sona	', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2470, 229, 2, 'One among three students - Vidyut, Manav and Ankit - is the winner of a quiz competition. Each one of them claims to have won the competition. It was also known that among them, there is one who always speaks the truth, one who always speaks lies and another whose statement cannot be considered as either true or false. The following are the statements made by them. <br>\r\nVidyut: I am not a Liar. <br>\r\nManav: I am a Liar. <br>\r\nAnkit: I neither speak the truth nor do I speak lies. <br>\r\nWho is the Liar? \r\n', 'Ankit 	', 'Manav		', 'Vidyut		', 'Indeterminate', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2471, 229, 2, 'One among three racers - Jatin, Lalit and Pandit - is the winner in the race. Each one of them claims that he was the winner. It was also known that among them, there is one who always speaks the truth, one who always speaks lies and another whose statement cannot be considered as either true or false. The following are the statements made by them. <br>\r\nJatin: I am not a Liar. <br>\r\nLalit: I am a Liar. <br>\r\nPandit: I neither speak the truth nor do I speak lies. <br>\r\n	Whose statement cannot be classified as either true or false? <br>', 'Jatin	', 'Lalit	', 'Pandit	', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2472, 229, 3, 'Four friends - Sameer, Haneef, Jayram and Puneet - sit around a square table, not necessarily in the same order. Exactly one person sits on each side and everyone is opposite to exactly one person. Each person makes two statements for any question asked to him. It was known that there is exactly one person who always speaks the truth and exactly one person who alternates between the truth and false. When asked about their respective positions around the table, the following were their replies: <br>\r\nSameer: Puneet sits opposite to me. Jayram sits to the left of Puneet. <br>\r\nHaneef: Sameer sits to my left. Puneet sits to the right of Jayram. <br>\r\nJayram: Haneef sits to my right. Puneet sits to my left. <br>\r\nPuneet: Jayram sits opposite to me. Haneef sits to my right. <br>\r\nIt was also known that a definite arrangement can be obtained by assessing their statements. <br>.	Who always speaks the truth?', 'Sameer ', 'Haneef	', 'Jayram	', 'Puneet', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2473, 229, 3, 'Four friends - Sid, Ben, James and Dan - sit around a circular table, not necessarily in the same order. Everyone is opposite to exactly one person. Each person makes two statements for any question asked to him. It was known that there is exactly one person who always speaks the truth and exactly one person who alternates between the truths and false. When asked about their respective positions around the table, the following were their replies: <br>\r\nSid: Dan sits to my left. Ben sits to the right of James. <br>\r\nBen: James sits opposite to me. Sid sits to my right. <br>\r\nJames: Sid sits to my right. Ben sits to my left. <br>\r\nDan: Ben sits opposite to me. James sits to the left of Ben. <br>\r\nIt was also known that a definite arrangement can be obtained by assessing their statements.\r\nWho among them are liars?', 'Sid and Dan ', 'Ben and James	', 'Ben and Dan ', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2474, 231, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Given are two statements followed by four conclusions numbered I, II and III. You have to take the two given statements to be true even if they seem to be variance with commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of them logically follows from the statements. <br>\r\n\r\n1.  	Statement I : All cups are spoons. <br>\r\n	Statement II : Some spoons are red. <br>\r\n	<b>Conclusions: </b> <br>\r\n	I. Some cups maybe red. <br>\r\n	II. All cups are red. <br>\r\n	III. No cup is red.\r\n', 'I', 'II', 'III', 'I and III', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2475, 231, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Given are two statements followed by four conclusions numbered I, II and III. You have to take the two given statements to be true even if they seem to be variance with commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of them logically follows from the statements. <br>\r\n\r\nStatement I : Both Vinod and Vinodini are shorter than Shama. <br>\r\n	Statement II : Shama is not the tallest of the four friends Vinod, Vinodini, Shama and Tara. <br>\r\n	<b>Conclusions: </b><br>\r\n	I. Tara is shorter than Vinod. <br>\r\n	II. Either Vinod or Vinodini is taller than Tara. <br>\r\n	III. Shama is the second tallest among the four friends. <br>', 'I', 'II', 'III', 'I and II', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2476, 231, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Given are two statements followed by four conclusions numbered I, II and III. You have to take the two given statements to be true even if they seem to be variance with commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of them logically follows from the statements. <br>\r\nStatement I : No woman is a sailor. <br>\r\n	Statement II : Lathika is a woman.	<br>	\r\n	<b>Conclusions: </b>	<br>\r\n	I.  Lathika is not a sailor. <br>\r\n	II. Lathika is a sailor. <br>\r\n	III. Only men are sailors.', 'only I', 'only II', 'I and II		', 'I and III', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2477, 231, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Given are two statements followed by four conclusions numbered I, II and III. You have to take the two given statements to be true even if they seem to be variance with commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of them logically follows from the statements. <br>\r\nStatement I : Some parrots are crows. <br>\r\n	Statement II: Some crows are sparrows. <br>\r\n	<b>Conclusions: </b>	<br>\r\n	I.  Some parrots are sparrows. <br>\r\n	II. No parrot is a sparrow. <br>\r\n	III. All sparrows are parrots.\r\n', 'I or II', 'II or III		', 'I or III	', 'II or III', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2478, 231, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Given are two statements followed by four conclusions numbered I, II and III. You have to take the two given statements to be true even if they seem to be variance with commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of them logically follows from the statements. <br>\r\nStatement I: All pens are pencils. <br>\r\n	Statement II : All pencils are scales. <br>\r\n	<b>Conclusions: </b>	<br>\r\n	I.  All pens are scales. <br>\r\n	II. All scales are pencils. <br>\r\nIII. All scales are pens.\r\n', 'only I', 'only II', 'I and II	', 'I, II and III', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2479, 231, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b> \r\n<br>Complete the following series.\r\n\r\n18, 19, 40, 123, â€¦\r\n', '496', '512', '372', '246', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2480, 231, 3, '<b>Directions for questions</b> <br>Complete the following series.\r\n5, 9, 25, 97, â€¦\r\n', '273', '384', '481', '577', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2481, 231, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b> <br>Complete the following series.\r\n\r\n2, 12, 30, 42, â€¦.\r\n', '120', '144', '72', '172', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2482, 231, 3, '<b>Directions for questions</b> <br>Complete the following series.\r\n 5, 10, 26, 50, â€¦.\r\n', '82', '92', '102', '122', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2483, 231, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b> <br>Complete the following series.\r\n1, 3, 4, 12, 16,â€¦\r\n', '40', '48', '64', '72', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2484, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>Each question is followed by two statements. You have to decide whether the information provided in the statements is sufficient for answering the question or not. <br>\r\nWho is the youngest among Gagan, Janak, Mona and Surya? <br>\r\n	A. Gagan is older than Janak. <br>\r\n	B. Mona and Janak are younger than Surya. <br>\r\n', 'Mark 1 If statement A alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement B alone. <br>', 'Mark 2 If statement B alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement A alone. <br>', 'Mark 3 If both the statements together are needed to answer the question but neither statement alone is sufficient. <br>', 'Mark 4 If both the statements together are not sufficient to answer the question. <br>', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2485, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>Each question is followed by two statements. You have to decide whether the information provided in the statements is sufficient for answering the question or not. <br>\r\nArjun took lesser time than Ram who took 45 minutes to complete the assignment. Did Vijay take more than 45 minutes to complete the asssignment? <br>\r\n	A. He took longer than Arjun. <br>\r\n	B. Arjun took 40 minutes <br>\r\n', 'Mark 1 If statement A alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement B alone. <br>', 'Mark 2 If statement B alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement A alone. <br>', 'Mark 3 If both the statements together are needed to answer the question but neither statement alone is sufficient. <br>', 'Mark 4 If both the statements together are not sufficient to answer the question. <br>', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2486, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>Each question is followed by two statements. You have to decide whether the information provided in the statements is sufficient for answering the question or not. <br>\r\nIs any Spartan smart? <br>\r\n	A. All Spartans are blonde. <br>\r\n	B. There is no blonde who is smart. <br>\r\n', 'Mark 1 If statement A alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement B alone. <br>', 'Mark 2 If statement B alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement A alone. <br>', 'Mark 3 If both the statements together are needed to answer the question but neither statement alone is sufficient. <br>', 'Mark 4 If both the statements together are not sufficient to answer the question. <br>', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2487, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>Each question is followed by two statements. You have to decide whether the information provided in the statements is sufficient for answering the question or not. <br>\r\nDid Vinod take his wallet? <br>\r\n	A. Vinod has money in his wallet. <br>\r\n	B. Vinod is going to buy a phone. <br>\r\n', 'Mark 1 If statement A alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement B alone. <br>', 'Mark 2 If statement B alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement A alone. <br>', 'Mark 3 If both the statements together are needed to answer the question but neither statement alone is sufficient. <br>', 'Mark 4 If both the statements together are not sufficient to answer the question. <br>', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2488, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>Each question is followed by two statements. You have to decide whether the information provided in the statements is sufficient for answering the question or not. <br>\r\nHow many of the students, in the class, are girls? <br>\r\n	A. The number of girls in the class is 20 less than the number of boys in the class<br>\r\n	B. The number of boys in the class is thrice the number of girls in the class. <br>\r\n', 'Mark 1 If statement A alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement B alone. <br>', 'Mark 2 If statement B alone is sufficient to answer the question, but not statement A alone. <br>', 'Mark 3 If both the statements together are needed to answer the question but neither statement alone is sufficient. <br>', 'Mark 4 If both the statements together are not sufficient to answer the question. <br>', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2489, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br> Each question has a main statement followed by four statements labeled A, B, C and D.  Choose the ordered pair of statements where the first statement implies the second, and the two statements are logically consistent with the main statement. <br>\r\nEither Madan is not intelligent, or he secures first rank. <br>\r\nA. Madan secures first rank. <br>\r\nB. Madan is not intelligent. <br>\r\nC. Madan does not secure first rank. <br>\r\nD. Madan is intelligent.\r\n', 'CB only', 'DA only', 'AB only', 'CB and DA', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2490, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br> Each question has a main statement followed by four statements labeled A, B, C and D.  Choose the ordered pair of statements where the first statement implies the second, and the two statements are logically consistent with the main statement. <br>\r\nEither Pallavi is pretty, or she is ugly. <br>\r\nA. Pallavi is ugly. <br>\r\nB. Pallavi is pretty. <br>\r\nC. Pallavi is not pretty. <br>\r\nD. Pallavi is not ugly.\r\n', 'CD only	', 'BA only	', 'CD & BA		', 'DB & CA', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2491, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br> Each question has a main statement followed by four statements labeled A, B, C and D.  Choose the ordered pair of statements where the first statement implies the second, and the two statements are logically consistent with the main statement. <br>\r\n\r\nWhenever Girish uses the cellphone, he gets a headache. <br>\r\nA. Girish did not get a headache. <br>\r\nB. Girish used the cellphone. <br>\r\nC. Girish got a headache. <br>\r\nD. Girish did not use the cellphone.\r\n', 'AD	', 'DC	', 'CB		', 'DA', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2492, 230, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br> Each question has a main statement followed by four statements labeled A, B, C and D.  Choose the ordered pair of statements where the first statement implies the second, and the two statements are logically consistent with the main statement. <br>\r\n\r\nIf I eat an apple, then I do not fall sick. <br>\r\nA. I ate an apple. <br>\r\nB. I did not fall sick. <br>\r\nC. I fell sick. <br>\r\nD. I did not eat an apple. <br>\r\n', 'AB only	', 'DC only', 'CD only	', 'AB and CD', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
