(2504, 233, 3, '<b>Directions for questions </b>: <br>These questions are based on the following data.\r\n<br>\r\nSeven women, Aliya, Jiren, Manju, Krithika, Pari, Dona and Sarah have parked their cycles in a row. The cycles of Pari and Dona should be next to each other. The cycles of Krithika and Sarah should be parked next to each other. Whereas Aliya and Jiren cannot park their cycles next to each other but Jiren and Krithika must park their cycles next to each other and Manju''s cycle is parked to the immediate right of Sarah''s cycle. <br>\r\nIf Aliya''s cycle is not next to Manju''s cycle, then what is the position of Aliyaâ€™s cycle from the right end of the row?\r\n', '1st', '7th ', '5th		', '1st or 7th ', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2505, 233, 3, '<b>Directions for questions </b>: <br>These questions are based on the following data.\r\n<br>\r\nSeven women, Aliya, Jiren, Manju, Krithika, Pari, Dona and Sarah have parked their cycles in a row. The cycles of Pari and Dona should be next to each other. The cycles of Krithika and Sarah should be parked next to each other. Whereas Aliya and Jiren cannot park their cycles next to each other but Jiren and Krithika must park their cycles next to each other and Manju''s cycle is parked to the immediate right of Sarah''s cycle. <br>\r\nIf Dona does not park her cycle next to Aliya''s, which is parked in the left extreme, then which of the following women can park their cycles between the cycles of Pari and Sarah?\r\n', 'Sarah, Manju and Jiren	', 'Aliya, Dona and Manju		', 'Dona, Sarah and Manju	', 'Dona, Jiren and Krithika', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
