(2509, 233, 2, '<b>Directions for questions </b>: <br> Read the information given below and then answer the questions that follow. <br>\r\n\r\nSeven books of subjects Algebra, Trigonometry, Geography, Astrophysics, Botany, Nutrition and Astrology have to be arranged in a row on a shelf in such a way that the Geography book and the Trigonometry book have only four books in between them, whereas the Algebra book is not in between the Geography and the Trigonometry books and the Botany book is to the immediate left of the Trigonometry book. <br>\r\n\r\nIf the Algebra and the Astrophysics books have two books between them, then which of these would be exactly in the middle of the row of books?	\r\n', 'Botany book', 'Astrophysics book	', 'Astrology book		', 'Nutrition book', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
