(2526, 235, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>These questions are based on the data given below. <br>\r\n\r\nGeorge, Emily, Rachel and Joey are four linguists. Each of them knows exactly two of the eight languages - French, Spanish, German, Hebrew, Italian, Hindi, Portuguese and Arabic - and each language is known by only one person. Rachel does not know Hindi and French, while Joey does not know German and Hebrew. Emily does not know Portuguese and Arabic, whereas George does not know Italian and Spanish. Arabic and Italian are known to neither Emily nor Rachel.\r\n\r\nIf Emily knows Hebrew and Spanish, then all the following could be true, except\r\n', 'Joey knows Hindi.', 'Rachel knows Portuguese and Italian.', 'George knows French.', 'Joey knows French.', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2527, 235, 2, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>These questions are based on the data given below. <br>\r\n\r\nGeorge, Emily, Rachel and Joey are four linguists. Each of them knows exactly two of the eight languages - French, Spanish, German, Hebrew, Italian, Hindi, Portuguese and Arabic - and each language is known by only one person. Rachel does not know Hindi and French, while Joey does not know German and Hebrew. Emily does not know Portuguese and Arabic, whereas George does not know Italian and Spanish. Arabic and Italian are known to neither Emily nor Rachel.\r\nIf Rachel knows Hebrew and Portuguese, Hindi is known neither to Joey nor to George and Arabic is not known to George then, all of the following could be TRUE, except\r\n', 'George knows German.', 'Joey knows Arabic and Italian.', 'George knows Hebrew.', 'Emily knows Spanish and Hindi.', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1);
