(2537, 235, 1, '<b>Directions for questions</b>: <br>These questions are based on the following data<br>\r\n\r\nFour brothers â€“ Amar, Ben, Craig and Dilip own four houses A, B, C and D respectively and two gadgets each. A rectangular plot was divided into four equal parts and the four houses were constructed. The gadgets are - Macbook, iPad, iPhone, Galaxy SII, Blackberry Storm, iPod, Dell Inspiron and Samsung Note. Macbook and iPad do not belong to the same person. Dilip has Samsung Note and Craig has iPod. Macbook and Blackberry Storm belong to brothers in adjacent houses A and B respectively. iPod does not belong to the person in the house diagonal to A. <br>\r\nIf the person with Macbook does not have Galaxy SII, then which of the following is definitely true?\r\n', 'iPod and iPad belong to the same person', 'Blackberry Storm and Galaxy SII belong to the same person', 'Samsung Note and iPhone belong to the same person', 'The person who owns Macbook also has either Dell Inspiron or iPhone.', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
