(2832, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\n\r\nA. Keraunophobia 	<br>	B. Tonitrophobia <br>\r\nC. Phonophobia 	<br>		D. Astraphobia\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2833, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\nA. HB <br>	B. ZU <br>		C. NI <br>		D. TO <br>\r\nE. PK\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2834, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\nA. Printer <br>			B. Author <br>\r\nC. Publisher<br> 			D. Correspondent <br>\r\nE. Reader\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(2835, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\nA. EQL<br> 	B. BHF 	<br>	C. KTI 	<br>	D. SXD <br>\r\nE. JWM\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2836, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\nA. Curd <br>	B. Butter <br>	C. Oil 	<br>	D. cream\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2837, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\nA. Poland <br>	B. Greece <br>	C. Spain <br>	D. Korea\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2838, 251, 2, '<B>Directions for Questions: </b><br> In each of the following questions one word is different from the rest. Find out the word which does not belong to the group<br>\r\nA. Copper<br> 	B. Tin 	<br>	C. Brass <br>	D. Zinc\r\n', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2839, 251, 2, 'Mr. A, Miss B, Mr. C and Miss D are sitting around a table and discussing their trades. <br>\r\nA. Mr. A sits opposite to cook <br>\r\nB. Miss b sits right to the barber. <br>\r\nC. The washer man is on the left of the tailor <br>\r\nD. Miss D sits opposite Mr. C<br>\r\nWhat are the trades of A and B?\r\n', 'Tailor and Barber ', 'Tailor and cook', 'Barber and cook ', 'Washerman and cook', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2840, 251, 2, 'In a pile of 10 books, there are 3 of History, 3 of Hindi, 2 of Mathematics and 2 of English. Taking from above, there is an English book between a History and Mathematics book, a History book between a Mathematics and an English book, a Hindi book between an English and a Mathematics book, a Mathematics book between two Hindi books and two Hindi books between a Mathematics and a History book. Book of which subject is at the sixth position from top? ', 'English ', 'Hindi	', 'Mathematics', 'History', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2841, 251, 2, 'On a man''s tombstone, it is said that one sixth of his life was spent in childhood and one twelfth as a teenager. One seventh of his life passed between the time he became an adult and the time he married; five years later, his son was born. Alas, the son died four years before he did. He lived to be twice as old as his son did. How old did the man live to be?', '84', '88', '81', '86', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2842, 251, 2, 'What two numbers have a product of 48 and, when the larger number is divided by the smaller, a quotient of 3?', '5, 15 	', '4, 12 	', '5, 12 	', '4, 15', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2843, 251, 2, 'A drove of sheep and chickens have a total of 99 heads and feet. There are twice as many chickens as sheep. How many of each are there?', 'Nine sheep and Eighteen chickens', 'Ten sheep and Nine chickens', 'Eighteen sheep and Ten chickens', 'Eighteen sheep and Eighteen chickens', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2844, 252, 2, 'Every day a cyclist meets a train at a particular crossing. The road is straight before the crossing and both are traveling in the same direction. The cyclist travels with a speed of 10 kmph. One day the cyclist comes late by 25 minutes and meets the train 5 km before the crossing. What is the speed of the train?', '60 kmph ', '50 kmph ', '70 kmph    ', '65 kmph', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2845, 252, 2, 'In a school, for a student out of 100 he got 74 of average for 7 subjects and he got 79 marks in the 8th \r\nsubject. What is the average of all the subject?\r\n', '76.251', '80.25', '74.265      ', '74.625', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2846, 252, 2, 'The ages of A and B are in the ration of 3:1. Fifteen years hence, the ratio will be 2:1. Their present ages are', '30 years, 10 years', '45 years, 15 years', '21 years, 7years', '60 years, 20 years', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2847, 252, 2, 'Fayiz is travelling on his cycle and has calculated to reach point A at 2 P.M. if he travels at 10 kmph, he will reach there at 12 noon if he travels at 15 kmph. At what speed must he travel to reach A at 1 P.M.?', '8 kmph', '11 kmph', '12 kmph    ', '14 kmph', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2848, 252, 2, 'A library has an average of 510 visitors on Sunday and 240 on other days. The average number of visitors per day in a month of 30 days beginning with a Sunday is', '250', '276', '280', '285', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2849, 252, 2, 'A boat moves upstream at the rate of 10 kms in 20 mins and downstream at the rate of 10 kms in 15 mins. The speed of the current is?', '10 kmph', '5 kmph', '15 kmph    ', '20 kmph', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2850, 252, 2, 'Two cogged wheels of which one has 32 cogs and other 54 cogs, work into each other. If the latter turns 80 times in three quarters of a minute, how often does the other turn in 8 seconds? ', '48', '135', '24', 'None', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2851, 252, 2, 'If there are 8 stations along a railway line, then how many different types of tickets must be printed so that the commuters can purchase a ticket from any one station to any other station?', '54', '66', '70', '76', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2852, 252, 2, 'A bath has two taps and a waste pipe. One of the taps on the own would fill the bath in ten minutes, the other would take a quarter of an hour, the waste pipe can empty a full bath in exactly seven and half minutes. Now if we start with an empty bath with both taps fully on, when (if ever) will the bath be full if the waste pipe is left open?', '15 min', '44 min', '22.5 min', '30 min', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(2853, 252, 2, 'In a production shop, 480 units were required to be produced. The supervisor had appointed 10 workers to do the job. However, some of them did not report for duty. As a result, each of those who were present, had to produce 72 units more than originally planned. How many workers did not report for work?', '4', '5', '6', 'None', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2854, 253, 2, '<b>Directions for questions:</b><br> Each problem consists of a problem followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Select your answer according to whether: <br> \r\nIf â€˜xâ€™ and â€˜yâ€™ are both positive integers, how much greater \r\nis â€˜xâ€™ than â€˜yâ€™? <br>\r\nI. x + y = 20 <br>			II. x = y2<br>\r\n', 'Statement I alone is sufficient, but statement II alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Statement II alone is sufficient, but statement I alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Both statements taken together are sufficient to answer the question, but neither statement alone is sufficient ', 'Each statement alone is sufficient ', 'Statements I and II together are not sufficient, and additional data is needed to answer the question ', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2855, 253, 2, '<b>Directions for questions:</b><br> Each problem consists of a problem followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Select your answer according to whether: <br> \r\nFifty percent of the articles in a certain magazine are \r\nwritten by staff members. Sixty percent of the articles are on \r\ncurrent affairs. If 75 percent of the articles on current affairs \r\nare written by staff members with more than 5 yearsâ€™ \r\nexperience of journalism, then how many of the articles on \r\ncurrent affairs are written by journalists with more than 5 \r\nyearsâ€™ experience? <br>\r\nI.	20 articles are written by staff members. <br>\r\nII. Of the articles on topics other than current affairs, 50 \r\npercent are by staff members with less than 5 yearsâ€™ \r\nexperience.\r\n', 'Statement I alone is sufficient, but statement II alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Statement II alone is sufficient, but statement I alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Both statements taken together are sufficient to answer the question, but neither statement alone is sufficient ', 'Each statement alone is sufficient ', 'Statements I and II together are not sufficient, and additional data is needed to answer the question ', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2856, 253, 2, '<b>Directions for questions:</b><br> Each problem consists of a problem followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Select your answer according to whether: <br> \r\nIs xy > 0? <br>\r\nI. x/y < 0 	<br>		II. x + y < 0\r\n', 'Statement I alone is sufficient, but statement II alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Statement II alone is sufficient, but statement I alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Both statements taken together are sufficient to answer the question, but neither statement alone is sufficient ', 'Each statement alone is sufficient ', 'Statements I and II together are not sufficient, and additional data is needed to answer the question ', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(2857, 253, 2, 'P, Q, R and S are playing a game of carom. P, R, and\r\n   S,Q are partners. S is to the right of R who is facing west.\r\n   Then which of the following direction is Q facing?\r\n\r\n', 'North ', 'South ', 'East', 'West', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2858, 253, 2, '<b> Directions for questions: <br>Refer the following \r\n   information to answer the question given below.</b><br>\r\nFive friends P, Q, R, S and T forward letters among\r\n    themselves in the following manner:  P sends letters to Q,\r\n    S and T. T sends letters to R, while P and R exchange\r\n    letters with each other. Q sends letters to S, who sends \r\n     letters to T. If P has to forward his letters to R, in how \r\n    many ways can the letters be forwarded?\r\n', 'Two', 'Three', 'Four', 'One', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(2859, 253, 2, '<b> Directions for questions: <br>Refer the following \r\n   information to answer the question given below.</b><br>\r\nFive friends A, B, C, D and E buy a book. They read the\r\n    book one after the other. A is the last person to read the \r\n    book. B or E can read the book only after D reads it. If E \r\n    gives the book to B after reading, who reads the book after\r\n    B and before A?\r\n', 'D', 'C', 'A', 'E', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2860, 253, 2, 'In a Blue Cross organisation, seven animals (two dogs \r\nA and B, two cats C and D, and three rabbits E, F and G are\r\nmade to sit in a row, in order to vaccinate. Exactly one animal\r\n(a dog) sits in between C and D. A alone sits in between G\r\nand E. No two animals of the same species sit next to each\r\nother. E sits to the immediate left of C. Who sits at the\r\nextreme left of the row?\r\n', 'G', 'E', 'F', 'C', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2861, 253, 2, '<b>Directions for questions:</b><br> Read the following\r\n   information carefully and answer the questions given it. <br><br>\r\n       Jayant, Kamal, Namitha, Asha and Tanmay are five  members of the family. They have their birth dates from January to May, each member in one of these months. Each one likes one particular item for his/her birthday out of Bengali Sweets, Chocolates, Pastries, Ice Cream and Dry Fruits. The one who likes Pastries is born in the month which is exactly middle in the months given. Asha does not like Ice cream but brings Chocolates for Jayant in February. Tanmay, who is fond of Bengali sweets, is born in the next month immediately after Namitha. Namita does not like Dry fruits or Ice cream <br><br>\r\nWhat is the choice of Asha? \r\n', 'Pastries ', 'Dry fruits ', 'Bengali Sweets       ', 'Indeterminate', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(2862, 253, 2, '<b>Directions for questions:</b><br> Read the following\r\n   information carefully and answer the questions given it. <br> <br>\r\n       Jayant, Kamal, Namitha, Asha and Tanmay are five  members of the family. They have their birth dates from January to May, each member in one of these months. Each one likes one particular item for his/her birthday out of Bengali Sweets, Chocolates, Pastries, Ice Cream and Dry Fruits. The one who likes Pastries is born in the month which is exactly middle in the months given. Asha does not like Ice cream but brings Chocolates for Jayant in February. Tanmay, who is fond of Bengali sweets, is born in the next month immediately after Namitha. Namita does not like Dry fruits or Ice cream <br> <br>\r\nWhich combination of month and item is true for Jayant? \r\n', 'March- Pastries ', 'February - Pastries ', 'February - Ice cream 	', 'None of these', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4605, 316, 2, 'The profit and loss statement for the financial year of a company shows a sale of Rs 15200. The primary cost is 25% of sales and leading costs account for 20% of the gross profit. The gross profit is determined by deducting the primary cost plus the cost of miscellaneous expenses of Rs 1200. The managing director''s salary of Rs 500 per annum plus 2% of annual sales is a minimum cost. What is the per cent profit on a capital investment of Rs 20000? ', '28%', '30%', '38%', '40%', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4435, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for the question: <br> Study the following table carefully to answer the questions that follow. </b><br>\r\nSemester fees (in Rs thousand) for five different courses in six different years <br>\r\nWhat was the approximate per cent increase in the semester fees of B Ed course in the year 2007 as compared to the previous year? \r\n', '26', '30', '20', '16', '10', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4436, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for the question: <br> Study the following table carefully to answer the questions that follow. </b><br>\r\nSemester fees (in Rs thousand) for five different courses in six different years <br>\r\nWhat was the average semester fee charged for MSc course over all the years together? \r\n', 'Rs. 12,700 ', 'Rs. 12,600 ', 'Rs. 12,060 ', 'Rs. 12070 ', 'Rs. 13,140 ', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4437, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for the question: <br> Study the following table carefully to answer the questions that follow. </b><br>\r\nSemester fees (in Rs thousand) for five different courses in six different years <br>\r\nWhat was the difference between the total semester fee charged for Diploma course over all the years together and the fee charged for B Tech course in the year 2009? \r\n', 'Rs. 8,500 ', 'Rs. 8,000 ', 'Rs. 6,500 ', 'Rs. 7,000 ', 'None of these', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4438, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for the question: <br> Study the following table carefully to answer the questions that follow. </b><br>\r\nSemester fees (in Rs thousand) for five different courses in six different years <br>\r\nThe semester fee charged for M Phil course in the year 2008 was approximately what percentage of the semester fee charged for MSc course in the year 2009? \r\n', '67', '84', '80', '76', '72', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4439, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for the question: <br> Study the following table carefully to answer the questions that follow. </b><br>\r\nSemester fees (in Rs thousand) for five different courses in six different years <br>\r\nWhat was the total semester fee charged for all the courses together in the year 2006?\r\n', 'Rs. 42,500 ', 'Rs. 41,500 ', 'Rs. 41,600 ', 'Rs. 42,200', 'None of these', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4442, 318, 2, 'Excluding stoppages, the speed of a bus is 54 kmph \r\nand including stoppages, it is 45 kmph. For how many \r\nminutes does the bus stop per hour?\r\n', '9', '10', '12', '20', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4443, 318, 2, 'A train can travel 50% faster than a car. Both start from \r\npoint A at the same time and reach point B 75 kms away \r\nfrom A at the same time. On the way, however, the train \r\nlost about 12.5 minutes while stopping at the stations. The \r\nspeed of the car is\r\n', '100 kmph', '110 kmph    ', '120 kmph    ', '130 kmph', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4444, 318, 2, 'For a body starting from rest, the distance travelled (D) \r\nis directly proportional to the square of the time elapsed \r\nfrom the start (t). When t = 4 sec, d = 48 m. What is the \r\nvalue of d (in m) at t = 6 sec?\r\n', '108', '144', '115', '147', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4445, 318, 2, 'The ratio between the three angles of a quadrilateral is 13 : 9 : 5 respectively. The value of the fourth angle of the quadrilateral is 36Â°. What is the difference between the largest and the second smallest angles of the quadrilateral? ', '104Â°', '108Â°', '72Â°', '96Â° ', 'None of these', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4446, 318, 2, '<b>Directions: Study the following pie-chart and bar chart and answer the following questions. </b><br>\r\n\r\nPercentage wise Distribution of students in six different Schools Total number of Students = 6000 Percentage of Students<br>\r\nNumber of Boys out of the 6000 Students in each School Separately<br>\r\nWhat is the total number of girls in School-C, number of girls in School-E and the number of boys in school-D together? \r\n', '1700', '1900', '1600', '1800', 'None of these ', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4447, 318, 2, '<b>Directions: Study the following pie-chart and bar chart and answer the following questions. </b><br>\r\n\r\nPercentage wise Distribution of students in six different Schools Total number of Students = 6000 Percentage of Students<br>\r\nNumber of Boys out of the 6000 Students in each School Separately<br>\r\nWhat is the respective ratio between the number of boys in School-C, number of girls in school-B and total number of students in School-E? \r\n', '45: 7: 97 ', '43: 9: 97 ', '45: 7: 87 ', '43: 9: 87 ', 'None of these ', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4448, 318, 2, '<b>Directions: Study the following pie-chart and bar chart and answer the following questions. </b><br>\r\n\r\nPercentage wise Distribution of students in six different Schools Total number of Students = 6000 Percentage of Students<br>\r\nNumber of Boys out of the 6000 Students in each School Separately<br>\r\nWhat is the difference between the total number of students in School-P and the number of boys in school-E? \r\n', '820', '860', '880', '900', 'None of these ', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4421, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for questions: <br> Each problem consists of a problem followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Select your answer according to whether: </b> <br><br>\r\nWhat is the value of y? <br>	\r\n I. y â€“ 3 = 2 <br>\r\nII. y2 = 25 \r\n', 'Statement I alone is sufficient, but statement II alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Statement II alone is sufficient, but statement I alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Both statements taken together are sufficient to answer the question, but neither statement alone is sufficient ', 'Each statement alone is sufficient ', 'Statements I and II together are not sufficient, and additional data is needed to answer the question', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4422, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for questions: <br> Each problem consists of a problem followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Select your answer according to whether: </b> <br><br>\r\nWhat was the percent increase of Company A''s stock between June 1 and June 30, 2000? <br> \r\nI. The stock gained $5 in value during June 2000. <br>\r\nII. The stock rose 12% during the first half of the month. \r\n', 'Statement I alone is sufficient, but statement II alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Statement II alone is sufficient, but statement I alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Both statements taken together are sufficient to answer the question, but neither statement alone is sufficient ', 'Each statement alone is sufficient ', 'Statements I and II together are not sufficient, and additional data is needed to answer the question', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4423, 316, 2, '<b>Directions for questions: <br> Each problem consists of a problem followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Select your answer according to whether: </b> <br><br>\r\nWhich company reported the larger dollar increase in earnings? <br> \r\nI. Company A reported that its earnings increased by 5%. <br>\r\nII. Company B reported that its earnings increased by 7%. \r\n', 'Statement I alone is sufficient, but statement II alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Statement II alone is sufficient, but statement I alone is not sufficient to answer the question ', 'Both statements taken together are sufficient to answer the question, but neither statement alone is sufficient ', 'Each statement alone is sufficient ', 'Statements I and II together are not sufficient, and additional data is needed to answer the question', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4424, 314, 2, 'Complete the series: 8 10 18 44 124 (?) ', '344', '366', '354', '356', 'None of these ', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4441, 318, 2, 'Pavan and Prateek can do a piece of work individually \r\nin 12 and 20 days respectively. They work together for a \r\nfew days before Pavan decides to leave. If it takes Prateek \r\n4 more days to complete the remaining work on his own, \r\nthen after how many days did Pavan leave?\r\n', '4', '14', '6', '3', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4426, 316, 2, 'Complete the series: 13 25 61 121 205 (?) ', '323', '326', '324', '313', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4427, 316, 2, 'Five-ninths of a number is equal to twenty five percent of the second number. The second number is equal to one-fourth of the third number. The value of the third number is 2960. What is 30 per cent of the first number? ', '88.8 ', '99.9 ', '66.6 ', 'Cannot be determined ', 'None of these', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4428, 316, 2, 'Dinesh''s monthly income is four times Suresh''s monthly income. Suresh''s monthly income is twenty per cent more than Jyoti''s monthly income. Jyoti''s monthly income is Rs. 22,000. What is Dinesh''s monthly income? ', 'Rs. 1, 06, 500 ', 'Rs. 1, 05, 600 ', 'Rs. 1, 04, 500 ', 'Rs. 1, 05, 400 ', 'None of these', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4429, 316, 2, 'Raju runs 1250 metre on Monday and Friday. Another days he runs 1500 metre except for Sunday (He does not run on Sunday). How many kilometre will he run in 3 weeks (first day starting from Monday)? ', '12.5km ', '20.5km ', '8.5km ', '25.5km ', 'None of these', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4430, 316, 2, 'In a school there are 250 students, out of whom 12 percent are girls. Each girl''s monthly fee is Rs. 450 and each boy''s monthly fee is 24 per cent more than that of a girl. What is the total monthly fee of girls and boys together?', 'Rs. 1, 36, 620 ', 'Rs. 1, 36, 260 ', 'Rs. 1, 32, 660 ', 'Rs. 1, 32, 460 ', 'None of these', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4431, 316, 2, 'The sum of nine consecutive odd numbers of Set A is 621. What is the sum of a different set of six consecutive even numbers whose lowest number is 15 more than the lowest number of Set A?', '498', '468', '478', '488', 'None of these', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4432, 316, 2, 'The ratio of the adjacent angles of a parallelogram is 7 : 8. Also, the ratio of the angles of quadrilateral is 5 : 6 : 7 : 12. What is the sum of the smaller angle of the parallelogram and the second largest angle of the quadrilateral? ', '168Â°', '228Â°', '156Â°', '224Â° ', 'None of these', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4433, 316, 2, 'A sphere with a diameter of 6 cm is dropped in a right circular cylindrical vessel that is partially filled with water. The diameter of the cylindrical vessel is 12 cm. If the sphere is completely submerged in water, how much will the level of water rise in the cylindrical vessel?', '1 cm ', '2 cm ', '3 cm ', '4 cm ', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4405, 316, 2, '<b>Directions: Study the following pie-chart and bar chart and answer the following questions. </b><br>\r\n\r\nPercentage wise Distribution of students in six different Schools Total number of Students = 6000 Percentage of Students<br>\r\nNumber of Boys out of the 6000 Students in each School Separately<br>\r\nWhat is the respective ratio between the number of boys in School-C, number of girls in school-B and total number of students in School-E? \r\n', '45: 7: 97 ', '43: 9: 97 ', '45: 7: 87 ', '43: 9: 87 ', 'None of these ', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4406, 316, 2, '<b>Directions: Study the following pie-chart and bar chart and answer the following questions. </b><br>\r\n\r\nPercentage wise Distribution of students in six different Schools Total number of Students = 6000 Percentage of Students<br>\r\nNumber of Boys out of the 6000 Students in each School Separately<br>\r\nWhat is the difference between the total number of students in School-P and the number of boys in school-E? \r\n', '820', '860', '880', '900', 'None of these ', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
