(3079, 264, 2, 'A police car moving at 45 kmph is chasing a thief who is traveling on a two wheeler at a speed of 30 kmph. The distance between the police car and the thief at 10:00 am is 48 kms. The car stops at 11:30 am for fifteen minutes to fill fuel and moves again at 45 kmph. In how much time after the police has started that they catch up with the thief?', '3 hrs. 30 min', '3 hrs. 57 min	', '3 hrs. 42 min	', '4 hrs. 01 min', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(3080, 264, 2, 'A tank has eight inlet taps to control inflow of water into the tank and four outlet taps to let water out of the tank. Each inlet tap can fill up the tank in 24 secs while it takes 35 secs to drain out the entire tank out of each outlet tap. If all the taps are opened for 4 secs when the tank is empty, what percentage volume of the tank gets filled?', '87.5 % ', '65 %	', '52.5 %    ', 'overflows', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(3081, 264, 2, 'The manufacturer sells an item to the distributor on a profit of 10%. The distributor marks up his cost price by 20% and then sells it to the retailer at 10% discount. The retailer does the same and sells it to the consumer. What % less would the consumer have paid, had he bought it from the manufacturer at Factory price?', '22.06% ', 'c', '23.08%', '30%', '', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(3082, 264, 2, 'A man bought 550 items at a total cost of Rs. 3685. 40% of the items were sold at a profit of 30 paise each. 220 items were sold at a loss of 4.48%. For the remaining, what should have been the selling price if he makes no profit and no loss?', 'Rs. 6.70 ', 'Rs. 6.50     ', 'Rs. 7   ', 'None of these', '', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(3083, 264, 2, 'A cask is filled with alcohol and water in the ratio 5 : 3.  16 gallons of this are drawn off and the cask is filled with water and then the proportion of alcohol to water becomes 3 : 5.  How many gallons does the cask hold?', '20', '30', '40', '50', '', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
