(4607, 321, 1, 'The following lines were overheard when six friends (Ayesha, Bhoomika, Chandra, Deepika, Emraan and Farhan) were discussing their ages at a party. <br>\r\n	(i)	Emraan to Chandra: â€œYou are older than me by 1/3rd my ageâ€. <br>\r\n	(ii) 	Bhoomika to Emraan: â€œI am younger than you by 1/6th your ageâ€. <br>\r\n	(iii)	Deepika to Bhoomika: â€œYou are elder to me by 2 yearsâ€. <br>\r\n	(iv)	Deepika also says â€œMy age is equal to 9/20th times the sum of ages of Ayesha and Emraanâ€. <br>\r\n	(v) 	Farhan finally reveals his age saying â€œI am 26 years oldâ€. <br>\r\n	Considering that all the above given statements are factually correct and also that the sums of ages of the first three (Ayesha, Bhoomika, Chandra) is equal to the sum of the ages of 	the last three (Deepika, Emraan and Farhan), by how many years is the oldest member elder than the youngest member of this group of six friends?  <br>\r\n', '12', '14', '16', '15', 'None of these', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
