(4625, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Each question is followed by two statements, A and B. Answer each question using the following instructions:<br>\r\n	Mark (1) if the question can be answered from statement A alone but not from statement B alone. <br>\r\n	Mark (2) if the question can be answered from statement B alone but not from statement A alone. <br>\r\n	Mark (3) if the question can be answered from statement A alone as well as from statement B alone. <br>\r\n	Mark (4) if the question can be answered from statements A and B together but not from either of them alone. <br>\r\n	Mark (5) if the question cannot be answered even from statements A and B together. <br><br>\r\n\r\nGiven that: 9x+17y=409, where x,y are positive integers. Is 3x>(2y+2) ? <br>\r\n	A. x is a prime number.<br> \r\n	B. y is an odd number.<br>\r\n', '1', '2', '3', '4', '5', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4626, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The table given below shows the average marks obtained by three different batches (10 a.m. to 1 p.m., 1 p.m. to 4 p.m., 4 p.m., to 7 p.m.,) in two sections â€œQuantitative abilityâ€ and â€œData Interpretationâ€ of 14 different MockCATs. The number of students in each of the three batches - were different, but across all the 14 tests held, the number of students in each batch remained constant. <br><br>\r\n\r\nFor how many tests can the average mark for these two sections for all the three batches combined be computed?\r\n', '6', '7', '8', '9', 'None of these', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4627, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The table given below shows the average marks obtained by three different batches (10 a.m. to 1 p.m., 1 p.m. to 4 p.m., 4 p.m., to 7 p.m.,) in two sections â€œQuantitative abilityâ€ and â€œData Interpretationâ€ of 14 different MockCATs. The number of students in each of the three batches - were different, but across all the 14 tests held, the number of students in each batch remained constant. <br><br>\r\n\r\nThe average mark for Data Interpretation across the 14 tests is highest for the batch(es)\r\n', '10 a.m. to 1 p.m.', '1 p.m. to 4 p.m.', '4 p.m. to 7 p.m.', 'Both (1) and (2)	', 'Both (2) and (3)', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4628, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The table given below shows the average marks obtained by three different batches (10 a.m. to 1 p.m., 1 p.m. to 4 p.m., 4 p.m., to 7 p.m.,) in two sections â€œQuantitative abilityâ€ and â€œData Interpretationâ€ of 14 different MockCATs. The number of students in each of the three batches - were different, but across all the 14 tests held, the number of students in each batch remained constant. <br><br>\r\n\r\nFor how many tests, is the average mark scored in Quantitative ability by three batches combined definitely more than that in Data Interpretation?\r\n', '2', '3', '4', '5', 'None of these', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4629, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The table given below shows the average marks obtained by three different batches (10 a.m. to 1 p.m., 1 p.m. to 4 p.m., 4 p.m., to 7 p.m.,) in two sections â€œQuantitative abilityâ€ and â€œData Interpretationâ€ of 14 different MockCATs. The number of students in each of the three batches - were different, but across all the 14 tests held, the number of students in each batch remained constant. <br><br>\r\n\r\nWhich of the following can possibly be the average mark for all the three batches combined in test 02, test 08 and test 11?\r\n', '52', '76', '84', '45', '87', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4630, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\nFor how many companies is the average investment per project greater than Rs. 10000 and the average time per project not more than 40 weeks?\r\n', '3', '4', '5', '6', 'None of these', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4631, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\nAssuming that all projects of company P is allocated to one company out of the other 15 companies, then which company could have the least investment per project?\r\n', 'N', 'E', 'C', 'J', 'O', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4632, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the average time per project for all the given 16 companies put together?\r\n', '47', '52', '68', '42', '31', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4633, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the total number of projects allocated to the company for which the value of the investment in the projects allocated to that company less the investment in the project the maximum value of that company is the highest?\r\n', '164', '109', '207', '392', '27', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4634, 321, 1, 'Directions for questions: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The bar graph which shows the viewership (by percentage) of four different channels A, B, C and D for a period of eight months is given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\n	It is known that the total viewership was higher in June over that of May. The total viewership was higher in November over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of August. The total viewership was higher in September over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of June. The total viewership was higher in December over that of November. The total viewership was higher in August over that of June. The total viewership was higher in November over that of September<br><br>\r\n\r\nIf the total number of people viewing channel A in July is J, the total numbers of people viewing channel C in June is T and the total number of people viewing channel B in August is P, then the relationship between J, T and P must be\r\n', 'J < P > T', 'T < J < P', 'J > T > P', 'T < J > P', 'J > T < P', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4635, 321, 1, 'Directions for questions: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The bar graph which shows the viewership (by percentage) of four different channels A, B, C and D for a period of eight months is given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\n	It is known that the total viewership was higher in June over that of May. The total viewership was higher in November over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of August. The total viewership was higher in September over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of June. The total viewership was higher in December over that of November. The total viewership was higher in August over that of June. The total viewership was higher in November over that of September<br><br>\r\n\r\nIf the total number of people viewing channel A in October is P, the total numbers of people viewing channel C in September  is F and the total number of people viewing channel B in December is J, then the relationship between P, F and J must be\r\n', 'J < P > F', 'P > J > F', 'J > F < P', 'J > F > P', 'None of these', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4636, 321, 1, 'Directions for questions: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The bar graph which shows the viewership (by percentage) of four different channels A, B, C and D for a period of eight months is given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\n	It is known that the total viewership was higher in June over that of May. The total viewership was higher in November over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of August. The total viewership was higher in September over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of June. The total viewership was higher in December over that of November. The total viewership was higher in August over that of June. The total viewership was higher in November over that of September<br><br>\r\n\r\nHow many occasions are there when the viewership of a channel decreased from one month to the next in-terms of percentage points?\r\n', '9', '10', '11', '12', 'None of these', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4637, 321, 1, 'Directions for questions: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The bar graph which shows the viewership (by percentage) of four different channels A, B, C and D for a period of eight months is given below. <br><br>\r\n\r\n	It is known that the total viewership was higher in June over that of May. The total viewership was higher in November over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of August. The total viewership was higher in September over that of October. The total viewership was higher in July over that of June. The total viewership was higher in December over that of November. The total viewership was higher in August over that of June. The total viewership was higher in November over that of September<br><br>\r\n\r\nIt is known that the total viewership was higher in May over that of November. If the total number of people viewing channel A, B and D respectively in July, May and October are F, P and T in the same order, then which of the following statement(s) is/ are always true?<br>\r\n	I. P > F			II. F > P		III. F > T		IV. P > T 		V. T > P\r\n', 'II, III and IV only', 'I, III and IV only', 'III and IV only', 'III and V only', 'None of these', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `qb_options` (`id`, `cat_id`, `difficulty_level`, `question`, `answer1`, `answer2`, `answer3`, `answer4`, `answer5`, `option1`, `option2`, `option3`, `option4`, `option5`, `status`) VALUES
(4638, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The total number of vehicles produced by the manufacturers B and D (in millions) is 35 and 30 vehicles respectively. The return on market value is defined as the ratio of operating profit and the Market Capitalisation. The total number of defects in the production of B, D and E (in millions) is 79.2, 64.5 and 89.2 respectively. The operating profit of the manufactures of A, D and E in (million Rs.) is 4, 6 and 8 respectively. The total time (in million man-hours) spent in manufacturing the vehicles by C and F are 560 and 630 respectively. The market capitalisation is the highest for the manufacture F. <br><br>\r\n\r\nWhich of the manufacturers has the highest operating profit in 2008?\r\n', 'B', 'D', 'E', 'F', 'Indeterminate', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4639, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The total number of vehicles produced by the manufacturers B and D (in millions) is 35 and 30 vehicles respectively. The return on market value is defined as the ratio of operating profit and the Market Capitalisation. The total number of defects in the production of B, D and E (in millions) is 79.2, 64.5 and 89.2 respectively. The operating profit of the manufactures of A, D and E in (million Rs.) is 4, 6 and 8 respectively. The total time (in million man-hours) spent in manufacturing the vehicles by C and F are 560 and 630 respectively. The market capitalisation is the highest for the manufacture F. <br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the total number of defects in the vehicles manufactured by F in 2008(in millions)?\r\n', '58.2 ', '59.4	', '65.3	', '58.4	', '58.8', 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1),
(4640, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The total number of vehicles produced by the manufacturers B and D (in millions) is 35 and 30 vehicles respectively. The return on market value is defined as the ratio of operating profit and the Market Capitalisation. The total number of defects in the production of B, D and E (in millions) is 79.2, 64.5 and 89.2 respectively. The operating profit of the manufactures of A, D and E in (million Rs.) is 4, 6 and 8 respectively. The total time (in million man-hours) spent in manufacturing the vehicles by C and F are 560 and 630 respectively. The market capitalisation is the highest for the manufacture F. <br><br>\r\n\r\nIf all manufacturers had an equal number of cumulative defects, then which of the manufacture had the least production in 2008?\r\n', 'C', 'B', 'F', 'D', 'Indeterminate', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4641, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	The total number of vehicles produced by the manufacturers B and D (in millions) is 35 and 30 vehicles respectively. The return on market value is defined as the ratio of operating profit and the Market Capitalisation. The total number of defects in the production of B, D and E (in millions) is 79.2, 64.5 and 89.2 respectively. The operating profit of the manufactures of A, D and E in (million Rs.) is 4, 6 and 8 respectively. The total time (in million man-hours) spent in manufacturing the vehicles by C and F are 560 and 630 respectively. The market capitalisation is the highest for the manufacture F. <br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the total time in million man-hours spent in manufacturing the vehicles of the company B in 2008?\r\n', '125', '420', '640', '720', 'Indeterminate', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1),
(4642, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	When, the number of goals scored by six different players participated in Fifa cup history was analysed, it is found that the difference of the squares of the number of goals scored by different three groups, each group, consisting two different players is 81. The highest number of goals is scored by Cristiano Ronaldo. The average of the number of goals scored by Ricardo Kaka and Michael Ballack is the number of goals scored by Pele. Ricardo Kaka has scored less number of goals compared to Michael Ballack. Kevin Keegan and Wayne Rooney are the two players considered in the list. .<br><br>\r\n\r\nIf Kevin Keegan scored the least number of goals then what is the number of goals scored by Wayne Rooney?\r\n', '40', '32', '28', '17', 'Indeterminate', 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4643, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	When, the number of goals scored by six different players participated in Fifa cup history was analysed, it is found that the difference of the squares of the number of goals scored by different three groups, each group, consisting two different players is 81. The highest number of goals is scored by Cristiano Ronaldo. The average of the number of goals scored by Ricardo Kaka and Michael Ballack is the number of goals scored by Pele. Ricardo Kaka has scored less number of goals compared to Michael Ballack. Kevin Keegan and Wayne Rooney are the two players considered in the list. .<br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the number of goals scored by Michael Balak?\r\n', '14', '16', '15', '17', 'Indeterminate', 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1),
(4644, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	When, the number of goals scored by six different players participated in Fifa cup history was analysed, it is found that the difference of the squares of the number of goals scored by different three groups, each group, consisting two different players is 81. The highest number of goals is scored by Cristiano Ronaldo. The average of the number of goals scored by Ricardo Kaka and Michael Ballack is the number of goals scored by Pele. Ricardo Kaka has scored less number of goals compared to Michael Ballack. Kevin Keegan and Wayne Rooney are the two players considered in the list. .<br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the average of the number of goals scored by Pele and Cristiano Ronaldo?\r\n', '22.5', '27', '31.5', '26', 'Indeterminate', 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1),
(4645, 321, 1, 'Directions for question: Refer the data given below to answer the following questions.<br><br>\r\n\r\n	When, the number of goals scored by six different players participated in Fifa cup history was analysed, it is found that the difference of the squares of the number of goals scored by different three groups, each group, consisting two different players is 81. The highest number of goals is scored by Cristiano Ronaldo. The average of the number of goals scored by Ricardo Kaka and Michael Ballack is the number of goals scored by Pele. Ricardo Kaka has scored less number of goals compared to Michael Ballack. Kevin Keegan and Wayne Rooney are the two players considered in the list. .<br><br>\r\n\r\nWhat is the position of Ricarda Kaka in-terms of the number of goals scored from the highest to the lowest?\r\n', '2', '3', '4', '5', 'Indeterminate', 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1);
